&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;preamble&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;reading time : 8 minutes&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Two weeks ago, I launched`capsule-gradle`— a plugin that transforms a deck reveal.js in WebM video capsule with TTS. Today, I&amp;#8217;m adding a new plugin: &lt;code&gt;hyperframes-gradle&lt;/code&gt;. It does something that capsule-gradle does not: transform the AsciiDoc &lt;strong&gt;directly&lt;/strong&gt; into an MP4 video, without going through reveal.js.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here&amp;#8217;s why this plugin exists, how it fits with the existing, and what HeyGen&amp;#8217;s HyperFrames engine brings to the content production pipeline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_hole_in_the_video_pipeline&quot;&gt;The Hole in the Video Pipeline&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My documentary pipeline produces two types of videos:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Revision capsule&lt;/strong&gt; (capsule-gradle) — a reveal.js deck captured as WebM with&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;narration TTS. Perfect for reviewing a module.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Animation Slides&lt;/strong&gt; (slider-gradle) — an interactive HTML reveal.js deck for&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;the in-person trainer&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But it lacks a third format: the &lt;strong&gt;standalone video&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 5.5555%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 5.5555%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 5.5555%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 5.5555%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 5.5555%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 5.5555%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 5.5555%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 5.5555%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 5.5555%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 5.5555%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 5.5555%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 5.5555%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 5.5555%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 5.5555%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 5.5555%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 5.5555%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 5.5555%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 5.5565%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;use case&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Current solution&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Lack&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Training slides&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;slider-gradle → reveal.js&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&amp;lt;/think&amp;gt; (output nothing)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Revision capsule&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;capsule-gradle → WebM&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;✅&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Teaser video&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;None&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;�❌&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Animated technical demo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;None&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;�❌&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Doc-to-video&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;None&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;❌&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The first use case is critical: how to generate automatically a 60-second video that presents a project or a module, with GSAP animations narration TTS, and musical background — everything from the same AsciiDoc file what about the slides?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Capsule-gradle cannot respond: it &lt;strong&gt;already&lt;/strong&gt; needs a reveal.js deck. slider-gradle produces this deck well, but it is not designed for video rendering. We needed a &lt;strong&gt;direct&lt;/strong&gt; pipeline: AsciiDoc → video.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_hyperframes_the_engine&quot;&gt;HyperFrames : The Engine&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I discoveredhttps://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes[HyperFrames] il y a a few days. It is an open-source framework (Apache 2.0) created by HeyGen, the unicorn of AI video. 22,700 stars on GitHub. The pitch fits in a phrase :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;quoteblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Write HTML. Render video. Built for agents.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The principle: you write HTML with`data-*`attributes, you reference a GSAP animation (or CSS, Lottie, Three.js…), and the engine renders everything in MP4 via Puppeteer (headless Chrome) + FFmpeg. Deterministic result: same input, same frames, same video.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-html hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;html&quot;&gt;&amp;lt;div id=&quot;stage&quot; data-composition-id=&quot;intro&quot; data-start=&quot;0&quot; data-width=&quot;1920&quot; data-height=&quot;1080&quot;&amp;gt;
  &amp;lt;video class=&quot;clip&quot; data-start=&quot;0&quot; data-duration=&quot;6&quot; data-track-index=&quot;0&quot;
         src=&quot;background.mp4&quot; muted playsinline&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/video&amp;gt;

  &amp;lt;h1 id=&quot;title&quot; class=&quot;clip&quot; data-start=&quot;1&quot; data-duration=&quot;4&quot; data-track-index=&quot;1&quot;&amp;gt;
    Formation Docker &amp;amp; Kubernetes
  &amp;lt;/h1&amp;gt;

  &amp;lt;audio data-start=&quot;0&quot; data-duration=&quot;6&quot; data-track-index=&quot;2&quot;
         data-volume=&quot;0.3&quot; src=&quot;music.wav&quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/audio&amp;gt;

  &amp;lt;script src=&quot;https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3/dist/gsap.min.js&quot;&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;
  &amp;lt;script&amp;gt;
    const tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });
    tl.from(&quot;#title&quot;, { opacity: 0, y: 40, duration: 0.8 }, 1);
    window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};
    window.__timelines.intro = tl;
  &amp;lt;/script&amp;gt;
&amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What makes HyperFrames different from Remotion? No React, no bundler, no JSX. Raw HTML that AI agents can write natively. It&amp;#8217;s tailored &lt;strong&gt;exactly&lt;/strong&gt; for my pipeline: planner-gradle with deepseek can generate this HTML from an SPG/SPD plan, and a Gradle plugin can convert it to MP4.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_architecture_of_the_plugin&quot;&gt;The Architecture of the Plugin&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;hyperframes-gradle follows the same pattern as all my plugins: the &lt;a href=&quot;0124_architecture_plugin_gradle_racine_consommateur_independant_post.html&quot;&gt;pattern « Independent Plugin + Consumer Root »&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-text hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;text&quot;&gt;hyperframes-gradle/
├── settings.gradle.kts          ← racine consommateur (dogfood)
├── build.gradle.kts              ← 3 lignes : apply plugin hyperframes
├── hyperframes-plugin/           ← BUILD INDÉPENDANT
│   ├── gradlew                    ← son propre wrapper
│   ├── build.gradle.kts           ← java-gradle-plugin
│   ├── src/main/kotlin/education/cccp/hyperframes/
│   │   ├── HyperframesPlugin.kt
│   │   ├── GenerateHyperframesHtmlTask.kt
│   │   ├── RenderHyperframesTask.kt
│   │   └── HyperframesExtension.kt
│   ├── .agents/                   ← gouvernance agent
│   └── doc/
│       └── HYPERFRAMES_ARCHITECTURE.adoc
└── video.yml                      ← configuration dogfood&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_four_step_pipeline&quot;&gt;The Four-Step Pipeline&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 8) ]

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontSize 11

title Pipeline hyperframes-gradle

rectangle &quot;AsciiDoc
source&quot; as adoc #LightYellow
^^^^^
 Syntax Error? (Assumed diagram type: activity)

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontSize 11

title Pipeline hyperframes-gradle

rectangle &quot;AsciiDoc
source&quot; as adoc #LightYellow
rectangle &quot;AsciidoctorJ&quot; as asciidoctorj #LightBlue
rectangle &quot;HTML HyperFrames
(data-* attributes)&quot; as html #LightGreen
rectangle &quot;HyperFrames CLI
(Node.js 22+)&quot; as cli #Lavender
rectangle &quot;video.mp4&quot; as mp4 #Gold

adoc -right-&amp;gt; asciidoctorj : parse blocs customs
asciidoctorj -right-&amp;gt; html : génère HTML
html -right-&amp;gt; cli : ProcessBuilder\nnpx hyperframes render
cli -right-&amp;gt; mp4 : Puppeteer + FFmpeg
@enduml&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AsciidoctorJ&lt;/strong&gt; parses the AsciiDoc source and extracts the custom blocks&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;[hyperframes-composition]&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;[hyperframes-track]&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;[hyperframes-animation]&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GenerateHyperframesHtmlTask&lt;/strong&gt; generates the HyperFrames HTML with the&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;`data-*`corresponding attributes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;RenderHyperframesTask&lt;/strong&gt; calls the HyperFrames CLI via`ProcessBuilder`:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;npx hyperframes render --input index.html --output video.mp4&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The MP4 is deployed in`output/`with a`metadata.json`for orchestration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_asciidoc_dsl&quot;&gt;The AsciiDoc DSL&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The real added value of the plugin is the AsciiDoc DSL. The user He never writes HTML. He annotates his existing AsciiDoc document :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-asciidoc hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;asciidoc&quot;&gt;= Formation Docker &amp;amp; Kubernetes
:hyperframes-width: 1920
:hyperframes-height: 1080
:hyperframes-fps: 30

[hyperframes-composition, id=&quot;intro&quot;]
== Introduction

Le titre apparaît avec un fondu GSAP sur fond vidéo.

[hyperframes-track, index=0, start=0, duration=6]
video::assets/background.mp4[muted, playsinline]

[hyperframes-track, index=1, start=1, duration=4]
Formation Docker &amp;amp; Kubernetes

[hyperframes-animation, type=gsap]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;const tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true }); tl.from(&quot;#title&quot;, { opacity: 0, y: 40, duration: 0.8 }, 1); window.&lt;em&gt;timelines = window.&lt;/em&gt;timelines || {}; window.__timelines.intro = tl;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The docinfo attributes`:hyperframes-width:`) set the dimensions. Custom blocks define the compositions and the tracks. The block `[hyperframes-animation]`contains the raw GSAP code — that the AI agent can generate from a natural language description.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_node_js_bridge&quot;&gt;The Node.js Bridge&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The only technical friction point: HyperFrames is in Node.js/TypeScript, and my plugins are in Kotlin/JVM. The solution is a`ProcessBuilder`:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;class RenderHyperframesTask : DefaultTask() {

    @TaskAction
    fun render() {
        val process = ProcessBuilder(
            &quot;npx&quot;, &quot;hyperframes&quot;, &quot;render&quot;,
            &quot;--input&quot;, inputHtml.absolutePath,
            &quot;--output&quot;, outputMp4.absolutePath
        )
            .inheritIO()
            .start()

        val exitCode = process.waitFor()
        require(exitCode == 0) {
            &quot;HyperFrames render failed with exit code $exitCode&quot;
        }
    }
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zero coupling between JVM code and Node.js. The contract is via the command line. and files on disk. It&amp;#8217;s the same pattern as`plantuml-gradle` (which calls the PlantUML CLI) or`slider-gradle`(who calls AsciidoctorJ). Nothing new under the sun — just applied to a newer tool.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_two_video_plugins_two_uses&quot;&gt;Two Video Plugins, Two Uses&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.7619%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 4.762%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;capsule-gradle&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;hyperframes-gradle&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Source&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Deck reveal.js (existing HTML)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;AsciiDoc → HTML HyperFrames&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Use case&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Revision capsule&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Standalone explanatory video&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Nature&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Slides → video&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Document → video&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Rendering&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Playwright Java → WebM&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;HyperFrames CLI → MP4&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Animation&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Transitions reveal.js natives&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;GSAP/CSS data-attributes&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Stack&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;100% JVM (Kotlin)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;JVM + external Node.js CLI&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;They don&amp;#8217;t replace each other. They complement each other. The complete value chain:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AsciiDoc ──→ slider-gradle ──→ deck reveal.js ──→ capsule-gradle ──→ WebM (revision capsule)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AsciiDoc ──→ hyperframes-gradle ──→ MP4 (standalone video)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The user writes a single AsciiDoc file. slider-gradle produces the slides. capsule-gradle produces the review capsule. hyperframes-gradle produces The teaser video and technical demos.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
