(github.com/anomalyco/opencode)&quot; as OC {
  rectangle &quot;vibe coding CLI
Open source, free&quot; as CLI
  note right of CLI
    C&#39;est l&#39;outil que j&#39;utilise
    pour coder avec des agents IA.
    Il ne fournit AUCUN modèle.
    C&#39;est un terminal + un orchestrateur.
  end note
}

package &quot;Ollama (Local Installation)&quot; as OL {
  rectangle &quot;Inference client
Installed on my machine&quot; as Client
  note right of Client
    C&#39;est le logiciel qui fait tourner
    les modèles. Il peut les exécuter
    en local OU les déléguer au cloud
    selon le tag (:cloud).
    Il s&#39;authentifie via clé SSH.
  end note
}

package &quot;Ollama Cloud
(ollama.com)&quot; as OCloud {
  rectangle &quot;Cloud inference service
Pro subscription: €20/month&quot; as Cloud
  note right of Cloud
    C&#39;est le fournisseur d&#39;inférence.
    Mes modèles avec le tag :cloud
    sont exécutés sur LEURS serveurs.
    L&#39;abonnement Pro donne accès
    à des quotas supérieurs.
  end note
}

Dev --&amp;gt; CLI : &quot;I type prompts&quot;
CLI --&amp;gt; Client : &quot;Call this model&quot;
Client --&amp;gt; Cloud : &quot;SSH key + request\n(models:cloud)&quot;
Client --&amp;gt; Client : &quot;Local execution
(models without :cloud)&quot;

@enduml&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock important&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-important&quot; title=&quot;❗&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OpenCode is NOT a model provider.&lt;/strong&gt;It&amp;#8217;s an open-source CLI (&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode&quot;&gt;github.com/anomalyco/opencode&lt;/a&gt;) that orchestrates AI agents. It does not sell a subscription, it does not provide inference. It is the equivalent of`git`for versioning: a tool, not a service. &lt;strong&gt;Ollama Cloud is the inference provider.&lt;/strong&gt;My local Ollama installation acts as &lt;strong&gt;client&lt;/strong&gt; — it authenticates with the Ollama servers via a unique SSH key (Device Key) and delegates execution of tagged models to them.&lt;code&gt;:cloud&lt;/code&gt;. The Pro subscription (20€/month) unlocks higher quotas and allows you to accumulate multiple accounts on the same machine via Docker.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_introduction_why_an_audit&quot;&gt;Introduction: Why an Audit?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Two months ago, I was using models for free on my local Ollama installation. Then I subscribed to a first Ollama Cloud Pro subscription at €20/month, which allows me to use the cloud models (those with the tag`:cloud`) via the provider`ollama-cloud`. A second subscription followed a month later, on a separate Docker instance with its own account and its own SSH key — the stacking method described in &lt;a href=&quot;0120_cumuler_deux_abonnements_ollama_pro_docker_post.html&quot;&gt;my article on stacking subscriptions&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The question that was bothering me: &lt;strong&gt;are these €20 per month justified?&lt;/strong&gt; Not by guesswork. With numbers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To answer, I needed precise data. Not estimates. Not averages. My &lt;strong&gt;actual&lt;/strong&gt; consumption, token by token, model by model, session by session.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And OpenCode — the CLI — stores all that in a SQLite database.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_opencode_database_a_gold_mine&quot;&gt;The OpenCode Database: A Gold Mine&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;OpenCode persists the entire history of its sessions in a SQLite file located at`~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db`. La mienne pèse 660 Mo pour 73 jours d&amp;#8217;utilisation — une base de données de production tout à fait respectable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ ls -lh ~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db
-rw-r--r-- 1 cheroliv cheroliv 660M mai 18 12:25 opencode.db&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_schema&quot;&gt;The Schema&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The database contains about twenty tables, but three of them are crucial for our audit:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/schema-principal.svg&quot; alt=&quot;schema principal&quot; width=&quot;684&quot; height=&quot;397&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The table`session`is perfect for a global audit: each session has its aggregated token count, its used model, and its cost. The field`model`is raw JSON :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-json hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;json&quot;&gt;{
  &quot;id&quot;: &quot;deepseek-v4-pro:cloud&quot;,
  &quot;providerID&quot;: &quot;ollama-cloud&quot;,
  &quot;variant&quot;: &quot;default&quot;
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock important&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-important&quot; title=&quot;❗&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The field`cost`The OpenCode database reflects only the &lt;strong&gt;external API fees&lt;/strong&gt; paid per consumption via API key (Google Gemini, OpenAI, etc.). Calls via Ollama — whether local or via Ollama Cloud Pro — are marked`cost=0`because the cost is flat-rate (subscription), not per-token. The real cost of these calls is the monthly subscription.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_extraction_code&quot;&gt;The Extraction Code&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No need to install anything. Node.js 22+ includes an experimental SQLite module (&lt;code&gt;node:sqlite&lt;/code&gt;) which works perfectly. Here is the script that gave me everything :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-javascript hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;javascript&quot;&gt;const { DatabaseSync } = require(&#39;node:sqlite&#39;);
const db = new DatabaseSync(
  `${process.env.HOME}/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db`,
  { readonly: true }
);

// 1. Statistiques globales
const global = db.prepare(`
  SELECT
    COUNT(*) as sessions,
    SUM(tokens_input) as total_input,
    SUM(tokens_output) as total_output,
    SUM(tokens_reasoning) as total_reasoning,
    SUM(tokens_cache_read) as total_cache_read,
    SUM(cost) as total_cost
  FROM session
`).get();

// 2. Ventilation par modèle et fournisseur
const byModel = db.prepare(`
  SELECT
    json_extract(model, &#39;$.id&#39;) as model_id,
    json_extract(model, &#39;$.providerID&#39;) as provider,
    COUNT(*) as sessions,
    SUM(tokens_input) as total_input,
    SUM(tokens_output) as total_output,
    SUM(cost) as total_cost
  FROM session
  WHERE model IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY model_id, provider
  ORDER BY SUM(tokens_input) DESC
`).all();

// 3. Par mois
const monthly = db.prepare(`
  SELECT
    strftime(&#39;%Y-%m&#39;, datetime(time_created/1000, &#39;unixepoch&#39;)) as month,
    COUNT(*) as sessions,
    SUM(tokens_input) as total_input,
    SUM(tokens_output) as total_output,
    SUM(cost) as total_cost
  FROM session
  WHERE time_created IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY month
  ORDER BY month
`).all();

// 4. Messages par modèle (détection des changements intra-session)
const msgByModel = db.prepare(`
  SELECT
    json_extract(m.data, &#39;$.model.providerID&#39;) as provider,
    json_extract(m.data, &#39;$.model.modelID&#39;) as model_id,
    COUNT(*) as messages
  FROM message m
  WHERE json_extract(m.data, &#39;$.model&#39;) IS NOT NULL
  GROUP BY provider, model_id
  ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC
`).all();

console.log({ global, byModel, monthly, msgByModel });
db.close();&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock note&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-note&quot; title=&quot;ℹ️&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The flag`--experimental-sqlite`is required on Node.js 22.x. On Node.js 24+, the module is stable and no longer requires a flag.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_results_73_days_of_consumption&quot;&gt;The Results: 73 Days of Consumption&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_global_view&quot;&gt;Global View&lt;/h3&gt;
