&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;gemini-2.5-flash @ google&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;211 K&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;19 K&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;\$0,04&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock important&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-important&quot; title=&quot;❗&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Three different providers for exactly the same DeepSeek V4 Pro model:
* &lt;code&gt;ollama-cloud&lt;/code&gt;→ via &lt;strong&gt;paid Pro subscription&lt;/strong&gt; (cloud managed by Ollama)
* &lt;code&gt;ollama-b&lt;/code&gt;→ &lt;strong&gt;second Pro subscription&lt;/strong&gt;, isolated in a distinct Docker container
* &lt;code&gt;ollama&lt;/code&gt;→ native locale instance, &lt;strong&gt;free&lt;/strong&gt; (runs directly on my machine)
The sum of the three gives 936M input, 8.4M output — that&amp;#8217;s my total consumption DeepSeek V4 Pro, all providers combined. Only`ollama-cloud`(220M input) costs a subscription. The remaining 716M are free (local or combined subscriptions).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_intra_session_models_what_the_session_table_does_not_see&quot;&gt;Intra-Session Models: What the Session Table Does Not See&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The table`session`only captures the session&amp;#8217;s &lt;strong&gt;primary&lt;/strong&gt; model. But during the same session, an OpenCode agent can switch between multiple models. The table`message`it reveals :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-text hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;text&quot;&gt;Modèles utilisés dans les messages (ollama-cloud provider) :
├─ deepseek-v4-pro      1 441 msgs  (32%)
├─ qwen3.5:397b         1 217 msgs  (27%)
├─ glm-5.1                712 msgs  (16%)
├─ kimi-k2.6:cloud        634 msgs  (14%)
├─ qwen3-coder:480b       414 msgs   (9%)
├─ gpt-oss:20b             34 msgs  (0,8%)
├─ qwen3-coder-next        27 msgs  (0,6%)
└─ gemma4:31b               7 msgs  (0,2%)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock caution&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-caution&quot; title=&quot;🔒&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I no longer use Qwen, GLM, Kimi, nor the other models. They appear in the history because I tested a lot of things in April. Since mid-May, I&amp;#8217;ve been locked onto DeepSeek V4 Pro — it&amp;#8217;s the only one that handles the load on long context with agent governance (cf. &lt;a href=&quot;0112_comparaison_kimi_glm_deepseek_long_contexte_plugin_gradle_opencode_post.html&quot;&gt;my comparison Kimi/GLM/DeepSeek&lt;/a&gt;). The 32% of deepseek messages in the history are misleading: today it&amp;#8217;s 100%.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_tariff_comparison_western_suppliers&quot;&gt;Tariff Comparison — Western Suppliers&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The thorny question: how much would this same consumption cost with traditional suppliers?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My calculation base for the comparison:&lt;strong&gt;220M tokens input + 1.9M tokens output&lt;/strong&gt;— &lt;strong&gt;only&lt;/strong&gt; the volume passed by`ollama-cloud`(the only one that matches my paid subscription). The remaining 716M are free (local Ollama and Docker B instance)&lt;/p&gt;
