&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_hidden_cost_prompt_engineering_and_iterations&quot;&gt;The Hidden Cost: Prompt Engineering and Iterations&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The token cost is only part of the equation. The real cost is developer time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With OpenCode + Ollama Cloud Pro + my agent governance (EAGER/LAZY/Hot/Warm/Cold, described in &lt;a href=&quot;0108_gouvernance_agent_opencode_eager_lazy_post.html&quot;&gt;the article on governance&lt;/a&gt;), I get:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;0 repetitive prompt engineering&lt;/strong&gt;: the context is injected automatically&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;90%+ first-shot correct&lt;/strong&gt;: the code compiles on the first try&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zero hallucination DeepSeek over 8 consecutive sessions&lt;/strong&gt;(documented in &lt;a href=&quot;0112_comparaison_kimi_glm_deepseek_long_contexte_plugin_gradle_opencode_post.html&quot;&gt;the Kimi/GLM/DeepSeek comparison&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With Claude or GPT &lt;strong&gt;without&lt;/strong&gt; fine-tune nor governance :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2-3 iterations per task on average&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Systematic prompt engineering&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hallucinations on Kotlin/Gradle APIs as soon as the context exceeds 30K tokens&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The monthly effective cost — tokens × iterations × correction time — is 27× to 54× that of my solution, as I demonstrated in &lt;a href=&quot;0122_ratio_efficacite_27x_45x_flotte_experts_ia_vs_claude_gpt_post.html&quot;&gt;the article on the efficiency ratio&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em&gt;_ It&amp;#8217;s not just about token price. A Claude Opus at 57× the price that requires 3× more iterations is an effective cost ~170× higher. To put it bluntly: paying an intern a McKinsey partner&amp;#8217;s salary. &lt;/em&gt;_&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_combine_ollama_cloud_pro_subscriptions_the_docker_method&quot;&gt;Combine Ollama Cloud Pro Subscriptions: The Docker Method&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If a single subscription isn&amp;#8217;t enough, we stack them. The principle is to isolate each subscription in its own Ollama installation, with its own SSH authentication key. Docker makes it trivial.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The complete method is detailed in &lt;a href=&quot;0120_cumuler_deux_abonnements_ollama_pro_docker_post.html&quot;&gt;the article on Docker accumulation&lt;/a&gt;, here is the principle:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 9) ]

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontSize 12

title Architecture — Two Ollama Cloud Pro Subscriptions on One Machine
left to right direction

node &quot;My Physical Machine&quot; {
  frame &quot;Ollama Instance A (native)
^^^^^
 Syntax Error? (Assumed diagram type: class)

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontSize 12

title Architecture — Two Ollama Cloud Pro Subscriptions on One Machine
left to right direction

node &quot;My Physical Machine&quot; {
  frame &quot;Ollama Instance A (native)
port:11434&quot; as Native {
    database &quot;Identity A
/usr/share/ollama/.ollama/id_ed25519&quot;
  }
  frame &quot;Ollama Instance B (Docker)
port :11435&quot; as Docker {
    database &quot;Identity B
~/ollama-b-data/id_ed25519&quot;
  }
}

cloud &quot;Ollama Cloud&quot; {
  actor &quot;Pro Account A
(email 1)&quot; as A
  actor &quot;Pro Account B
(email 2)&quot; as B
}

Native --&amp;gt; A : &quot;Device Key A&quot;
Docker --&amp;gt; B : &quot;Device Key B&quot;

note bottom of Docker
  Conteneur Docker isolé :
  - Clé SSH distincte
  - Port réseau distinct (11435)
  - Volume persistant (~/ollama-b-data)
  - restart: always
end note
@enduml&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pattern is simple:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create a volume`~/ollama-b-data`&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Run a Docker container`ollama/ollama:0.20.2`mapped onto`11435:11434`&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Retrieve the SSH key from the container → save it on ollama.com&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Do`ollama signin`with a second email&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Configure OpenCode with two providers (`ollama`on :11434,`ollama-b`on :11435)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Two accounts, one blue card, zero conflict.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_what_the_audit_does_not_measure&quot;&gt;What the Audit Does Not Measure&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 40%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 60%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;Blind spot&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;Impact&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality of the produced code&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;2.6 billion tokens do not say whether the code compiles. My 8 DeepSeek V4 Pro sessions have a first-shot rate &amp;gt;90%.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OpenCode ecosystem&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;CLI is free, but its value (agents, sandboxes, history, prompt caching) is immense. It is not included in the subscription price — it is a separate tool.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Opportunity cost&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Spending 2 hours a day debugging hallucinations of an inferior model costs more than €20/month.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Peace of mind&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Flat rate = no surprise. With per‑token pricing, an activity spike can really hurt.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock warning&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-warning&quot; title=&quot;⚠️&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The quoted prices are those of May 2026. In six months, everything will have decreased. But the structural balance of power — fixed subscription vs pay‑per‑use — will remain favorable to subscription for heavy consumers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_conclusion_the_verdict_of_numbers&quot;&gt;Conclusion: The Verdict of Numbers&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After 73 days, 1,022 OpenCode sessions, and 2.6 billion tokens:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 60%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 40%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;Metric&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;Verdict&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Cumulative external API cost&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;\$0.22&lt;/strong&gt;(almost null)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Ollama Cloud Pro subscription cost&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;~20€/month&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Equivalent Claude Opus&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;$1,148/month&lt;/strong&gt;— 57× more expensive&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Equivalent GPT 5.5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;\$1 157/month&lt;/strong&gt;— 58× more expensive&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Equivalent HuggingFace/Novita&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;$374/month&lt;/strong&gt;— 19× more expensive&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Direct DeepSeek API equivalent&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;$390/month&lt;/strong&gt;— 20× more expensive&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Cheapest equivalent (Gemini Flash)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;$69/month&lt;/strong&gt;— 3.5× more expensive, lower model&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Best offer on the market&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ollama Cloud Pro at 20€/month&lt;/strong&gt;— unbeatable&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;__&lt;/em&gt; At €20 per month to access DeepSeek V4 Pro (1.6T params, MoE, CSA+HCA, 1M context) via Ollama Cloud, I have the best value for money on the global market. Even Chinese providers directly are 5× to 20× more expensive. Even HuggingFace, with its aggregation of low-cost providers, is 19× more expensive. The Western market (Claude, GPT) is at 50-60× — another planet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This ratio is so imbalanced that it cannot last forever. Enjoy it while it exists. &lt;em&gt;__&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Well yes, my 20 bucks a month is the best technical investment of my life as a developer. And now you have the numbers to prove it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
