&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_anatomy_of_the_name_plugin_subfolder&quot;&gt;Anatomy of the &lt;code&gt;{name}-plugin/&lt;/code&gt; subfolder&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;sectlevel2&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_the_version_catalog_two_distinct_files&quot;&gt;The Version Catalog: Two Distinct Files&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_what_we_do_not_do&quot;&gt;What we do not do&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_comparison_the_three_architectures_facing_dogfooding&quot;&gt;Comparison : The Three Architectures Facing Dogfooding&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_the_dag_contract_a_root_build_never_comes_from_a_subfolder&quot;&gt;The DAG Contract: A Root Build Never Comes From a Subfolder&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_conclusion_the_apparent_duplication_that_saves_time&quot;&gt;Conclusion : The Apparent Duplication That Saves Time&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_references&quot;&gt;References&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;preamble&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;reading time : 11 minutes&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You clone a Gradle plugin repository. You open a terminal. What do you type next?&lt;code&gt;./gradlew tasks&lt;/code&gt;, of course. But in which folder? The root? The sub-module? Should one first read a README to know how to build? If you hesitate, wouldn’t in a second, the project architecture is broken.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here&amp;#8217;s how I solved this problem once and for all — and why this pattern is today the signature of all my Gradle plugins in`foundry/public/`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_problem_three_architectures_that_made_me_waste_time&quot;&gt;The Problem: Three Architectures That Made Me Waste Time&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before converging to the current pattern, I groped between three approaches Classic ways to organize a Gradle plugin. Each had a fatal flaw.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_option_1_the_isolated_plugin_no_dogfooding&quot;&gt;Option 1: The Isolated Plugin (no dogfooding)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The project contains only the plugin. No example of consumption. No project that it exercises. To test it, you must create an external project, y reference the plugin via`mavenLocal`or a composite build, and only there check that it works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-shell hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;shell&quot;&gt;$ git clone mon-plugin
$ cd mon-plugin
$ ./gradlew build          # le plugin compile
$ # ... et maintenant ? comment je l&#39;essaie ?&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock warning&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-warning&quot; title=&quot;⚠️&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A Gradle plugin without a consumption example is a library without integration tests. You never know if the latest change a broken the user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_option_2_the_monorepo_classic_includeplugin&quot;&gt;Option 2: The Monorepo Classic (&lt;code&gt;include(&quot;:plugin\&quot;)&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gradle`init`generates`settings.gradle.kts`with`include(&quot;plugin&quot;)`. The root and the sub-module share the same daemon, the same configurations, the same catalogs. Practical, but coupled.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-text hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;text&quot;&gt;.
├── settings.gradle.kts   → include(&quot;plugin&quot;)
├── build.gradle.kts      → plugins { id(&quot;mon-plugin&quot;) }
├── plugin/
│   └── build.gradle.kts  → java-gradle-plugin
└── gradle/
    └── libs.versions.toml&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What&amp;#8217;s the snag:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The root&lt;strong&gt;must&lt;/strong&gt;have the same Gradle version as the submodule.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;`libs.versions.toml`is shared — common version catalogs, dependencies&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;who flee from one module to another&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cannot build the plugin independently of the root.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The CI must build the two modules, even if only the plugin has changed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_option_3_the_composite_build_includebuild_the_composite_build&quot;&gt;Option 3: The Composite Build (&lt;code&gt;includeBuild()&lt;/code&gt;) The Composite Build&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We separate the two into distinct Gradle builds and we connect them via &lt;code&gt;includeBuild(&quot;mon-plugin&quot;)`in`settings.gradle.kts&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is already better. The plugin build is isolated. But the consumer must explicitly reference the external build — and the output of `./gradlew tasks`at the root depends on the proper configuration of the composite. Cloning is not zero-config : you need to know that the plugin is in a separate folder, the root references it, etc.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-shell hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;shell&quot;&gt;.
├── settings.gradle.kts   → includeBuild(&quot;plugin-build/&quot;)
├── build.gradle.kts      → plugins { id(&quot;mon-plugin&quot;) }
└── plugin-build/
    ├── settings.gradle.kts
    └── build.gradle.kts&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I was looking for better. Much better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_solution_two_independent_builds_one_consumer_root&quot;&gt;The Solution: Two Independent Builds, One Consumer Root&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here is the pattern I ended up adopting:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-text hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;text&quot;&gt;.
├── settings.gradle.kts          ← racine consommateur
├── build.gradle.kts              ← 3 lignes : apply plugin + dogfood
├── gradle/
│   └── libs.versions.toml        ← catalogue du consommateur
├── {name}-plugin/                ← BUILD INDÉPENDANT
│   ├── gradlew                    ← son propre wrapper
│   ├── settings.gradle.kts        ← rootProject.name = &quot;{name}-plugin&quot;
│   ├── build.gradle.kts           ← java-gradle-plugin, signing, publish
│   ├── gradle/
│   │   ├── libs.versions.toml     ← catalogue du plugin
│   │   └── wrapper/
│   ├── src/                       ← sources du plugin
│   ├── .agents/                   ← gouvernance agent
│   └── *.adoc                     ← AGENT, PROMPT_REPRISE, snapshot, etc.
└── site.yml / slides-context.yml / ...   ← configs dogfood&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock important&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-important&quot; title=&quot;❗&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The key :`{name}-plugin/`is a fully self-contained Gradle project. It has its own wrapper, its own settings, its own catalog of versions. It clones, builds, tests, and publishes itself without the root be aware of his/her existence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The root, on the other hand, only does &lt;strong&gt;one&lt;/strong&gt; thing: apply the plugin.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;plugins {
    alias(libs.plugins.bakery)
}

repositories {
    mavenLocal()
    mavenCentral()
}

bakery { configPath = file(&quot;site.yml&quot;).absolutePath }&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Three lines in the case of`bakery-gradle`. Nothing more. Zero`include()&lt;code&gt;, zero`includeBuild()&lt;/code&gt;, zero subproject. A classic Gradle build that applies a plugin like any Which consumer would do that?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_workflow&quot;&gt;The Workflow&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/architecture-deux-builds.svg&quot; alt=&quot;architecture deux builds&quot; width=&quot;1277&quot; height=&quot;151&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_concrete_workflow&quot;&gt;The Concrete Workflow&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-shell hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;shell&quot;&gt;# 1. Builder le plugin
$ cd codebase-plugin
$ ./gradlew publishToMavenLocal

# 2. L&#39;exercer depuis la racine
$ cd ..
$ ./gradlew indexCodebase queryCodebase snapshot

# La boucle est fermée. Le plugin est testé dans des conditions
# réelles de consommation, par le projet même qui l&#39;héberge.&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_why_this_architecture_won_me_over&quot;&gt;Why This Architecture Won Me Over&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Three benefits that, combined, are worth the cost of &#39;duplication&#39;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_native_dogfooding_instant_feedback&quot;&gt;Native Dogfooding, Instant Feedback&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The best test of a Gradle plugin is to use it. Not a mocked unit test. Not a`GradleRunner`with a project of test. A &lt;strong&gt;real&lt;/strong&gt; build that applies the plugin on real files.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-shell hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;shell&quot;&gt;$ git clone bakery-gradle
$ cd bakery-gradle
$ ./gradlew bake    # ← le plugin est exercé immédiatement&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If the plugin is broken, the root build says so. No need to go look for an external test project. Dogfooding is the &lt;strong&gt;first&lt;/strong&gt; Task that a new contributor launches. It is the definitive smoke test.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock tip&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-tip&quot; title=&quot;💡&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The rule is simple: if the root compiles and that`./gradlew tasks` Displays your plugin tasks, the plugin is functional. No surprise. in production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_2_zeroconfig_cloning&quot;&gt;2. Zero‑config cloning&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Un `git clone &amp;amp;&amp;amp; ./gradlew tasks`and the newcomer sees everything walk without configuring anything. The`build.gradle.kts`root is the living usage documentation of the plugin. The`site.yml`next to shows the expected configuration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compare with the alternative: a three‑paragraph README that explain how to build the plugin and how to build the project of test. A new contributor skims the README, is mistaken, opens an issue—while the information could to be &lt;strong&gt;executable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock important&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-important&quot; title=&quot;❗&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The most robust documentation isn&amp;#8217;t the one that is read. It&amp;#8217;s the one that we&lt;strong&gt;execute&lt;/strong&gt;. The root build is the documentation plugin executable&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_3_isolated_builds_independent_ci&quot;&gt;3. Isolated Builds, Independent CI&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The plugin has its own Gradle wrapper, its own lifecycle, its own tests. You can:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Upgrade Gradle in the plugin without touching the root&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Add a dependency in the plugin without it leaking into the root&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Break the plugin without impacting the root build (as long as you don&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Don&amp;#8217;t publish the broken version)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Having a CI that builds/tests the plugin, and another that exercises the&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;root — independently&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-text hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;text&quot;&gt;.github/workflows/
├── test-plugin.yml      → codebase-plugin/.gradlew build
├── test-root.yml        → .gradlew tasks (vérifie que le plugin est consommable)
└── publish.yml          → codebase-plugin/.gradlew publish&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_anatomy_of_the_name_plugin_subfolder&quot;&gt;Anatomy of the &lt;code&gt;{name}-plugin/&lt;/code&gt; subfolder&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Let’s take a closer look at what lives in the plugin folder:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-text hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;text&quot;&gt;codebase-plugin/
├── gradlew                           ← wrapper indépendant
├── settings.gradle.kts               ← @Suppress(&quot;UnstableApiUsage&quot;)
│                                       + foobar-resolver-convention
├── build.gradle.kts                  ← java-gradle-plugin + signing + publish
├── gradle/
│   ├── libs.versions.toml            ← catalogue complet (langchain4j, pgvector...)
│   └── wrapper/
├── buildSrc/                         ← classes utilitaires buildSrc
│   ├── build.gradle.kts
│   └── src/main/kotlin/
│       ├── codebase/                 ← CodebaseYmlAnonymizer, CodebaseConfiguration
│       ├── benchmark/                ← BenchmarkConfig, BenchmarkProtocol
│       ├── readme/                   ← ReadmeYmlAnonymizer
│       ├── site/                     ← SiteYmlAnonymizer
│       ├── slider/                   ← SliderYmlAnonymizer
│       └── snapshot/                 ← SnapshotManager
├── src/
│   ├── main/kotlin/codebase/
│   │   ├── CodebasePlugin.kt         ← class Plugin&amp;lt;Project&amp;gt;
│   │   ├── rag/                      ← pgvector, embedding, anonymization...
│   │   ├── benchmark/                ← BenchmarkRunner, export, comparison...
│   │   └── walker/                   ← WorkspaceWalker
│   └── test/
│       ├── kotlin/codebase/scenarios/ ← steps Cucumber
│       ├── features/                  ← .feature files
│       └── resources/datasets/        ← fixtures .adoc, .yml, .json
├── .agents/                          ← gouvernance agent (INDEX, SESSIONS, etc.)
├── AGENT.adoc                        ← règles agent
├── PROMPT_REPRISE.adoc              ← mission session
├── BACKLOG.adoc                      ← backlog produit
├── snapshot.adoc                     ← snapshot auto-généré du projet
└── embeds.yml                        ← config RAG embeds&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Everything is here. No dispersion between the root and the subfolder. The developer working on the plugin never needs to leave`codebase-plugin/`. The developer who uses the plugin only looks at the root — and the`build.gradle.kts`of 3 lines Tell him everything he needs to know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_version_catalog_two_distinct_files&quot;&gt;The Version Catalog: Two Distinct Files&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 25%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 37.5%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 37.5%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;gradle/libs.versions.toml&lt;/code&gt;(root)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;{name}-plugin/gradle/libs.versions.toml&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Number of dependencies&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;2-3 (plugin + optionally readme)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;30+ (langchain4j, pgvector, cucumber&amp;#8230;&amp;#8203;)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Role&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Consume the plugin&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Build the plugin&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Who reads it&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;The plugin user&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;The plugin developer&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The root has an intentionally minimal catalog. The plugin has a catalog complete. Confusion is impossible: each build has its own scope of dependencies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock note&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-note&quot; title=&quot;ℹ️&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have already spent an hour debugging a dependency collision between your plugin and your test project, you understand the value of this separation. Independent catalogs eliminate this problem by construction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_what_we_do_not_do&quot;&gt;What we do not do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This pattern is not magical. It imposes a constraint that I willingly inflicts on me:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Root does not build the plugin.&lt;/strong&gt; You must`publishToMavenLocal` ou deploy on a repository before the root can consume it&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It&amp;#8217;s a minimal cost, and it&amp;#8217;s the &lt;strong&gt;right&lt;/strong&gt; constraint. The root consumes the plugin as an external client — via Maven. Exactly as a third-party project would. If the plugin is not publishable, the root tells you immediately.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-shell hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;shell&quot;&gt;# La seule &quot;friction&quot; du pattern
$ cd codebase-plugin &amp;amp;&amp;amp; ./gradlew publishToMavenLocal &amp;amp;&amp;amp; cd ..
$ ./gradlew tasks --group=codebase&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_comparison_the_three_architectures_facing_dogfooding&quot;&gt;Comparison : The Three Architectures Facing Dogfooding&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 20%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 20%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 20%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 20%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 20%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Isolated plugin&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Monorepo`include()`&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Composite`includeBuild()`&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Root + independent plugin.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;`git clone &amp;amp;&amp;amp; gradlew tasks`gives the tasks of the plugin&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;�❌&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;[No French text was provided for translation. The input contained only instructions and a checkmark symbol, which is not French text to translate.]&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;✅&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;✅&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Root-independant build plugin&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;�✅&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;�❌&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;✅&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;✅&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Separate catalogue versions&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;✅&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;❌&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;✅&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;�✅&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;No`include()` ni &lt;code&gt;includeBuild()&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;✅&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;�❌&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;�❌&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;�✅&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Native dogfood without configuration&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;�❌&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;✅&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;⚠️&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;�✅&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Independent CI plugin&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;✅&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;❌&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;✅&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;✅&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Root is an example of real consumption&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;❌&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;⚠️&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Could you please provide the French text to translate?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;�✅&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The right column checks all the boxes. That&amp;#8217;s why I don&amp;#8217;t I will go further back.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_dag_contract_a_root_build_never_comes_from_a_subfolder&quot;&gt;The DAG Contract: A Root Build Never Comes From a Subfolder&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This architecture naturally integrates into the DAG N0→N3 of my workspace. The pattern is: &lt;strong&gt;plugin N2 is the hub From its own dependencies, the N3 root is a terminal who applies hubs&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/contrat-dag-architecture.svg&quot; alt=&quot;contrat dag architecture&quot; width=&quot;1742&quot; height=&quot;5508&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Le &lt;code&gt;codebase-gradle/build.gradle.kts`is 6 lines. No`src/&lt;/code&gt;, no`buildSrc/&lt;code&gt;, no`gradle/rag-bench.gradle.kts&lt;/code&gt;. Just &lt;code&gt;plugins { alias(libs.plugins.codebase) }`and the repositories. All the complexity lives in`codebase-plugin/&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_conclusion_the_apparent_duplication_that_saves_time&quot;&gt;Conclusion : The Apparent Duplication That Saves Time&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When I show this structure to someone, the first reaction is often: &quot;But you have two`gradlew`, two`settings.gradle.kts`, two`libs.versions.toml`— this is duplication !&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Yes. And no.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Duplication is reproducing the same information in two places. Here, these are two &lt;strong&gt;distinct&lt;/strong&gt; files serving two &lt;strong&gt;distinct&lt;/strong&gt; uses : the plugin catalog (30+ dependencies for builder) and the catalog from the root (2-3 dependencies to consume). The plugin wrapper (locked version for development) and the root wrapper (potentially different version, for the exercise of the plugin).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It&amp;#8217;s not duplication. It&amp;#8217;s &lt;strong&gt;separation of responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt; applied to the build system. Each build It does one thing, and only one. The root consumes. The plugin builds itself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The cost? An order`publishToMavenLocal`between the build of the plugin and the build of the root. The gain? An architectural clarity that Eliminates hours of downstream debugging.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since I deployed this pattern on`bakery-gradle`, &lt;code&gt;plantuml-gradle&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;codebase-gradle&lt;/code&gt;, and the other plugins of`foundry/public/&lt;code&gt;, I don&amp;#8217;t have I never again hesitated when opening a terminal in one of my repositories. The first reflex —&lt;/code&gt;./gradlew tasks`— still walking, still giving the good tasks, and instantly tells me if everything is healthy&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That&amp;#8217;s it, good architecture. It cannot be read in a README. It is experienced in a terminal, in less than ten seconds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
