&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;preamble&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This guide explains step by step how to install the &lt;strong&gt;kitty&lt;/strong&gt; terminal on Xubuntu, configure it correctly, and replace bash with &lt;strong&gt;zsh&lt;/strong&gt; as the default shell. The kitty project is available here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/kovidgoyal/kitty&quot; class=&quot;bare&quot;&gt;https://github.com/kovidgoyal/kitty&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;__&lt;/em&gt; Kitty is a modern, fast, and configurable terminal, particularly suited to demanding developers. &amp;lt;/think&amp;gt; (Empty output)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_why_choose_kitty_and_zsh&quot;&gt;Why choose Kitty and Zsh?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kitty is distinguished by:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Superior performance thanks to GPU acceleration,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A configuration entirely based on a single text file,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An excellent support for fonts and ligatures&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zsh, for its part, is a powerful interactive shell offering:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An intelligent completion,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A customizable prompt,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Great compatibility with bash.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By combining Kitty and Zsh, you benefit from a productive and aesthetic environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/kitty-zsh-overview.png&quot; alt=&quot;kitty zsh overview&quot; width=&quot;729&quot; height=&quot;305&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock note&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-note&quot; title=&quot;Note&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This guide is deliberately limited to installation via script and Xubuntu.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_system_prerequisites&quot;&gt;System prerequisites&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before you start, make sure you have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Xubuntu installed,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;internet access,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;a functional bash shell to launch the script&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check your environment:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;uname -a
lsb_release -a&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_download_and_installation_of_kitty&quot;&gt;Download and installation of Kitty&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kitty recommends installing it via an official script that places the files in`~/.local/kitty.app`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock important&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-important&quot; title=&quot;Important&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This method is independent of package managers (no`apt`).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_download_the_installation_script&quot;&gt;Download the installation script&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Execute the following command:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;curl -L https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/installer.sh | sh /dev/stdin&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This command performs:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;downloading the binaries,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;extraction in`~/.local/kitty.app`,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;creation of the symbolic links.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/download-install.svg&quot; alt=&quot;download install&quot; width=&quot;301&quot; height=&quot;336&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_creation_of_symbolic_links&quot;&gt;Creation of symbolic links&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In order to be able to invoke`kitty`from the terminal, create a symbolic link :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;ln -s ~/.local/kitty.app/bin/kitty ~/.local/bin/kitty&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Add`~/.local/bin`Add to your PATH if it&amp;#8217;s not already done:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;echo &#39;export PATH=&quot;$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH&quot;&#39; &amp;gt;&amp;gt; ~/.zshrc
source ~/.zshrc&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can check the installation:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;kitty --version&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_integration_of_kitty_in_xubuntu&quot;&gt;Integration of Kitty in Xubuntu&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For Kitty to appear in the applications menu:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_copy_the_desktop_file&quot;&gt;Copy the desktop file&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Copy the file`.desktop`provided :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;cp ~/.local/kitty.app/share/applications/kitty.desktop ~/.local/share/applications/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_edit_the_desktop_file&quot;&gt;Edit the desktop file&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Edit the file:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;nano ~/.local/share/applications/kitty.desktop&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check or modify the following lines:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;[Desktop Entry]
Version=1.0
Type=Application
Name=Kitty Terminal
Comment=Fast GPU-based terminal emulator
Exec=/home/$USER/.local/kitty.app/bin/kitty
Icon=kitty
Categories=System;TerminalEmulator;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Replace`YOURUSER`by your username.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/desktop-integration.png&quot; alt=&quot;desktop integration&quot; width=&quot;448&quot; height=&quot;335&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_set_kitty_as_the_default_terminal_optional&quot;&gt;Set Kitty as the default terminal (optional)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So that Kitty is the default terminal:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;sudo update-alternatives --install /usr/bin/x-terminal-emulator x-terminal-emulator ~/.local/kitty.app/bin/kitty 50
sudo update-alternatives --config x-terminal-emulator&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Select`kitty`in the proposed menu.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_installation_of_zsh&quot;&gt;Installation of Zsh&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If Zsh is not yet installed, run:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;sudo apt install zsh&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check the installation:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;zsh --version&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_set_zsh_as_default_shell&quot;&gt;Set Zsh as default shell&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can change your shell globally or only in Kitty.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_global_method_for_all_terminals&quot;&gt;Global method (for all terminals)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify the absolute path:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;which zsh&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In general`/usr/bin/zsh`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Change the default shell:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;chsh -s /usr/bin/zsh&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Log out and then log back in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/zsh-default-shell.svg&quot; alt=&quot;zsh default shell&quot; width=&quot;546&quot; height=&quot;341&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_kitty_specific_method&quot;&gt;Kitty-specific method&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you prefer to only change the shell in Kitty, edit the configuration file:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;nano ~/.config/kitty/kitty.conf&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Add this line:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-text hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;text&quot;&gt;shell zsh&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Save and restart Kitty.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_configuration_of_zsh_optional&quot;&gt;Configuration of Zsh (optional)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To customize your Zsh:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_create_a_zshrc_file&quot;&gt;Create a .zshrc file&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;touch ~/.zshrc
nano ~/.zshrc&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_example_of_minimal_configuration&quot;&gt;Example of minimal configuration&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;export ZSH_THEME=&quot;robbyrussell&quot;
export PATH=&quot;$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH&quot;
alias ll=&quot;ls -la&quot;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_summary_of_the_complete_workflow&quot;&gt;Summary of the complete workflow&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The diagram below summarizes the whole process:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/full-workflow.png&quot; alt=&quot;full workflow&quot; width=&quot;354&quot; height=&quot;643&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_final_verification&quot;&gt;Final verification&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Launch Kitty :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;kitty&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You should see that`zsh`is active :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;echo $SHELL&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Expected result:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;/usr/bin/zsh&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To change the font size in&lt;strong&gt;Kitty&lt;/strong&gt;, it is necessary to adjust the parameter`font_size`in the configuration file. Here is the detailed procedure:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_open_the_configuration_file&quot;&gt;📂 Open the configuration file&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The main configuration file is usually located in :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;~/.config/kitty/kitty.conf&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this file does not yet exist, you can create it. Example :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;nano ~/.config/kitty/kitty.conf&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_️_add_or_modify_font_size&quot;&gt;�🖋️ Add or modify `font_size&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Add the following directive, or modify it if it already exists:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-text hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;text&quot;&gt;font_size 14.0&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here`14.0`matches the desired size. You can set any decimal value, for example`12.0`, &lt;code&gt;15.5&lt;/code&gt;, etc.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_save_and_restart_kitty&quot;&gt;💾 Save and restart Kitty&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Save (&lt;code&gt;Ctrl + O&lt;/code&gt;, then`Entrée`) and leave (&lt;code&gt;Ctrl + X&lt;/code&gt;) if you are using`nano`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Close all Kitty windows, then restart the terminal for the change to take effect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_dynamic_adjustment_temporary_zoom&quot;&gt;✅ Dynamic adjustment (Temporary zoom)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want to temporarily zoom in/out without changing the settings, use the default keyboard shortcuts:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Increase the font size&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Ctrl + Shift + =&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Decrease the font size&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Ctrl + Shift + -&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reset the size&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;Ctrl + Shift + Backspace&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These settings do not persist after the terminal is closed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_installation_and_configuration_of_oh_my_zsh&quot;&gt;Installation and configuration of Oh My Zsh&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Once Zsh is installed and configured as your default shell, you can enrich your environment with &lt;strong&gt;Oh My Zsh&lt;/strong&gt;, a framework for managing Zsh configuration, offering:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;a collection of themes for the prompt,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;many plugins,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;a clear organization of the configuration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_installation_of_oh_my_zsh&quot;&gt;Installation of Oh My Zsh&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Make sure that Zsh is active:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;zsh --version&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If necessary, launch:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;zsh&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Then download and run the official installation script:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;sh -c &quot;$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ohmyzsh/ohmyzsh/master/tools/install.sh)&quot;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This script :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;creates the folder`~/.oh-my-zsh`,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Optionally save your file`~/.zshrc`,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;automatically activates the new prompt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_change_the_theme&quot;&gt;Change the theme&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Open your configuration file:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;nano ~/.zshrc&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Modify the variable`ZSH_THEME`to choose another theme (for example`agnoster`):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ZSH_THEME=&quot;agnoster&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Save then reload the configuration:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;source ~/.zshrc&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_verification&quot;&gt;Verification&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Launch Kitty and verify that the prompt has changed correctly. You can confirm that Oh My Zsh is active by executing:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;echo $ZSH&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The result should be similar to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;/home/your_user/.oh-my-zsh&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_use_case_diagram&quot;&gt;Use case diagram&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/ohmyzsh-installation.png&quot; alt=&quot;ohmyzsh installation&quot; width=&quot;521&quot; height=&quot;480&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_enable_translucency_in_kitty&quot;&gt;Enable translucency in Kitty&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;One of Kitty&amp;#8217;s most appreciated features is the ability to add &lt;strong&gt;transparency&lt;/strong&gt; to the terminal background. This allows you to faintly see the underlying environment (window, desktop, etc.), which is particularly useful for multitasking.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_prerequisites_for_transparency&quot;&gt;Prerequisites for transparency&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Transparency in Kitty is based on the&lt;strong&gt;window composer&lt;/strong&gt;used by the graphical environment. On Xubuntu (based on XFCE), make sure that the&lt;strong&gt;composition is activated&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;To verify :&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;right-click on the desktop &amp;gt; Settings &amp;gt;&lt;strong&gt;Window manager settings&lt;/strong&gt;,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;tab&lt;strong&gt;Composer&lt;/strong&gt;: the &lt;code&gt;Activer la composition&lt;/code&gt; box must be checked.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/transparency-usecase.png&quot; alt=&quot;transparency usecase&quot; width=&quot;600&quot; height=&quot;217&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_configuration_of_transparency_in_kitty_conf&quot;&gt;Configuration of transparency in kitty.conf&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Open your configuration file`~/.config/kitty/kitty.conf`&amp;lt;/think&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;nano ~/.config/kitty/kitty.conf&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Add or modify the following lines:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-conf hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;conf&quot;&gt;background_opacity 0.85&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This parameter accepts values between:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;1.0&lt;/code&gt;→ opaque (no transparency),&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;0.0&lt;/code&gt;→ completely transparent (unusable)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;intermediate values like`0.90`, &lt;code&gt;0.75&lt;/code&gt;, etc.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A good visual compromise is usually between`0.85` et &lt;code&gt;0.95&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_restart_kitty&quot;&gt;Restart Kitty&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Close all instances of Kitty, then launch a new window for the changes to take effect:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;kitty&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_possible_complements&quot;&gt;Possible complements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you use a custom terminal background, you can also set a background color with transparency (in RGBA):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-conf hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;conf&quot;&gt;background #1e1e2eff&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The last component`ff`) indicates the opacity (of`00` à &lt;code&gt;ff&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_sequence_diagram_kitty_initialization_with_transparency&quot;&gt;Sequence diagram - Kitty initialization with transparency&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/transparency-sequence.png&quot; alt=&quot;transparency sequence&quot; width=&quot;771&quot; height=&quot;422&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_known_limitations&quot;&gt;Known limitations&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock warning&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-warning&quot; title=&quot;Warning&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Translucency does not work if : - the XFCE compositor is disabled, - an incompatible window manager is being used, - you are using Kitty in a &lt;strong&gt;tmux&lt;/strong&gt; mode in the background without transparency support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_disable_the_audible_bell&quot;&gt;Disable the audible bell&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By default, Kitty emits a &lt;strong&gt;beep&lt;/strong&gt; sound when an erroneous command is entered or a terminal event triggers it. This noise can quickly become annoying, especially in an intensive development environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To disable this behavior, add the following directive to the file`~/.config/kitty/kitty.conf`:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-conf hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;conf&quot;&gt;audible_bell no&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock note&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-note&quot; title=&quot;Note&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can also enable a &lt;strong&gt;visual feedback&lt;/strong&gt; instead of the beep sound with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-conf hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;conf&quot;&gt;visual_bell yes&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_update_of_kitty&quot;&gt;Update of Kitty&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since Kitty is installed via a script and not a package manager, updating is done by rerunning the official installation script. This allows you to download the latest version and update your existing installation in`~/.local/kitty.app`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock note&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-note&quot; title=&quot;Note&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The suffix`.app`in the path`~/.local/kitty.app`is the Kitty installation convention on Linux via its official script, and in no way indicates exclusive compatibility with macOS.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock important&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-important&quot; title=&quot;Important&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before running the update command, make sure you are in your home directory (&lt;code&gt;~&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Run the following command from your home directory:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;curl -L https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/installer.sh | sh /dev/stdin&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This script will handle:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Download the binaries of the new version.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Extract the files in`~/.local/kitty.app`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Update symbolic links if necessary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After the update, it is recommended to close all instances of Kitty and restart them to ensure that the new version is properly taken into account.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_references&quot;&gt;References&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you wish to delve deeper into customization, see the official documentation :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Kitty: &lt;a href=&quot;https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/&quot; class=&quot;bare&quot;&gt;https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/conf/#opt-kitty.background_opacity&quot; class=&quot;bare&quot;&gt;https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/conf/#opt-kitty.background_opacity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/conf/#opt-kitty.audible_bell&quot; class=&quot;bare&quot;&gt;https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/conf/#opt-kitty.audible_bell&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zsh: &lt;a href=&quot;https://zsh.sourceforge.io/&quot; class=&quot;bare&quot;&gt;https://zsh.sourceforge.io/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Github: &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/kovidgoyal/kitty&quot; class=&quot;bare&quot;&gt;https://github.com/kovidgoyal/kitty&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zsh: &lt;a href=&quot;https://zsh.sourceforge.io/&quot; class=&quot;bare&quot;&gt;https://zsh.sourceforge.io/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ohmyz.sh/&quot; class=&quot;bare&quot;&gt;https://ohmyz.sh/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/ohmyzsh/ohmyzsh/wiki&quot; class=&quot;bare&quot;&gt;https://github.com/ohmyzsh/ohmyzsh/wiki&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfwm4/compositor&quot; class=&quot;bare&quot;&gt;https://docs.xfce.org/xfce/xfwm4/compositor&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_conclusion&quot;&gt;Conclusion&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You now have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;of a modern and high-performance terminal (Kitty)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;of a powerful and customizable shell (Zsh)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;of a clean configuration independent of system packages&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;of an aesthetic and functional terminal equipped with Oh My Zsh&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

