&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The verdict is harsh. For inference:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ollama Pro&lt;/strong&gt;: he would make you&lt;strong&gt;23 years&lt;/strong&gt;to amortize a DGX Spark. The Spark will have been obsolete for 20 years.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ollama Max&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;strong&gt;4 years&lt;/strong&gt;— provided you use Spark 24/7, which nobody does&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Claude Pro&lt;/strong&gt;: same problem,&lt;strong&gt;20 years&lt;/strong&gt;for a closed single-model&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em&gt;_ The promise of the &quot;desktop AI supercomputer&quot; runs up against an elementary accounting reality: $4,699 / $20 per month = never profitable for individual use. &lt;/em&gt;_&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_even_with_intensive_usage&quot;&gt;Even with intensive usage&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;#8217;s take the worst-case scenario for the cloud: you run an H100 8 hours per day, 5 days per week, 52 weeks per year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;8 × 5 × 52 = 2,080 hours/year&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;2 080 × $2/h (average spot price H100) =&lt;strong&gt;$4,160/year&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Spark ($4 699) is paid off in&lt;strong&gt;13 months&lt;/strong&gt;. Except that:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The H100 is&lt;strong&gt;~10x faster&lt;/strong&gt;That the Spark&amp;#8217;s GB10. You do in 1h what Spark does in 10h. For the same volume of work, the H100 costs you $416 per year, not $4,160.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Le H100 a 80 Go HBM à 3.35 To/s de bande passante. Le Spark a 128 Go LPDDR5X à 273 Go/s. Pour les gros modèles, la bande passante compte plus que la capacité.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock important&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-important&quot; title=&quot;❗&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comparing 1 hour of H100 to 1 hour of Spark makes no sense. The H100 does the work 10x faster. The true cloud cost for a given workload is therefore ~10x lower than the naive calculation based on hours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_fine_tuning_the_cloud_is_unbeatable&quot;&gt;Fine-Tuning: The Cloud Is Unbeatable&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The classic argument of Spark&amp;#8217;s defenders: &quot;yes but for fine-tuning, it&amp;#8217;s different&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No, it isn&amp;#8217;t.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_real_cost_of_a_fine_tune&quot;&gt;The real cost of a fine-tune&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A LoRA/QLoRA fine-tune on Unsloth of a 7B model:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;~2-3h on an H100 =&lt;strong&gt;$5 to $9&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Same thing on the Spark =&lt;strong&gt;20-30h&lt;/strong&gt;(10x slower), blocks the machine&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With Spark&amp;#8217;s $4,699, you can finance:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;~500 to ~900 fine-tunes&lt;/strong&gt;in cloud H100&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ou &lt;strong&gt;~23 years&lt;/strong&gt;of Ollama Pro&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ou &lt;strong&gt;~4 years&lt;/strong&gt;of Ollama Max&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And for larger models (70B+):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Le Spark avec ses 128 Go peut charger un 70B en Q4 — mais le fine-tune sera extrêmement lent&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Un H100 avec 80 Go peut fine-tuner un 70B en QLoRA 4-bit en quelques heures&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For full fine-tuning, you need multi-GPU anyway — Spark is out of the race&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_specialized_actors&quot;&gt;The Specialized Actors&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2026, platforms such as Unsloth, Modal, Replicate, and Together AI offer serverless fine-tuning:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No GPU management&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No environment configuration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Payment by the minute&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Integrated optimizations (flash attention, automatic quantization)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;diag-fine-tuning-cost&quot; class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/diag-plantuml-md5-a0a8d04a43a5cb90ab62f5246deb54b8.svg&quot; alt=&quot;Comparaison des coûts de fine-tuning&quot; width=&quot;626&quot; height=&quot;244&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_only_true_reason_data_sovereignty&quot;&gt;The Only True Reason: Data Sovereignty&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After eliminating inference, fine-tuning, and cost-effectiveness — what remains for Spark?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Absolute confidentiality&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not privacy: &quot;I don&amp;#8217;t want my prompts to be read by an OpenAI employee&quot;. That&amp;#8217;s a non-issue in 2026: Ollama, Groq, and most reputable providers have zero-log and zero-retention policies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;True confidentiality is:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory air-gap&lt;/strong&gt;defense, diplomacy, health — the data cannot &lt;strong&gt;physically&lt;/strong&gt; leave the building&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Critical proprietary data&lt;/strong&gt;: source code of an unpublished product, trade secrets, trading algorithms&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Network resilience&lt;/strong&gt;: The AI must continue to function even if the Internet goes down&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock caution&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-caution&quot; title=&quot;🔒&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But let&amp;#8217;s be honest: what percentage of DGX Spark buyers actually fall into this case? 1%? The rest is &#39;nice to have&#39; turned into a $4,699 expense.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_true_calculation_of_privacy&quot;&gt;The True Calculation of Privacy&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For individual use:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ollama Pro&lt;/strong&gt;($20/month) + Chinese open-source models = pragmatic solution&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If a prompt leaks at Ollama, it gets lost among the millions of daily requests. It&amp;#8217;s a drop in the ocean.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The real risk is not the leak of a prompt — it&amp;#8217;s the non-consensual training on your data. Serious providers contractually prohibit this.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em&gt;_ The fear of &quot;distilling one&amp;#8217;s prompt into the LLM&quot; is a level of personal information propagation so diluted that it is more anxiety than a real threat. On an industrial scale, it is different. But on an individual scale, it is noise. &lt;/em&gt;_&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
