&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_automatic_gdpr_classification_the_llm_as_router&quot;&gt;Automatic GDPR Classification: the LLM as Router&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_roadmap_from_asciidoc_to_langgraph4j&quot;&gt;Roadmap: from AsciiDoc to LangGraph4j&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_what_this_architecture_solves_and_what_it_does_not_solve&quot;&gt;What This Architecture Solves (and what it does not Solve)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_conclusion_architecture_as_discourse&quot;&gt;Conclusion: Architecture as Discourse&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_references&quot;&gt;References&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;preamble&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;reading time : 20 minutes&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prompt engineering is fragile. At 80,000 tokens, your alignment rules are drowned in the noise, and the LLM forgets what you asked it at the beginning of the conversation. My solution? Don&amp;#8217;t align by text, but by l&#39;&lt;strong&gt;space&lt;/strong&gt;. I have structured my development workspace into four concentric circles of trust — from the intimate secret garden to the public forges — and each circle is a physical area of the file system. The LLM does not need to be reminded of the rules: the file path contains them. Here’s how it works, and why this spatial alignment architecture is more resilient than a`system prompt`of 500 lines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It&amp;#8217;s a long article.&lt;br&gt;
Get comfortable&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;dlist&quot;&gt;
&lt;dl&gt;
&lt;dt class=&quot;hdlist1&quot;&gt;tick&lt;/dt&gt;
&lt;dd&gt;
&lt;p&gt;[]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/dd&gt;
&lt;/dl&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_observation_prompt_engineering_is_a_sand_castle&quot;&gt;The Observation: Prompt Engineering is a Sand Castle&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For three weeks, I developed Gradle plugins with Opencode, using three different LLMs — Kimi K2.6, GLM-5.1, and DeepSeek-V4-Pro (the sole survivor, but that&amp;#8217;s another story&lt;a href=&quot;0112_comparaison_kimi_glm_deepseek_long_contexte_plugin_gradle_opencode_post.html&quot;&gt;Already covered here.&lt;/a&gt;) My agent governance method&lt;a href=&quot;0108_gouvernance_agent_opencode_eager_lazy_post.html&quot;&gt;I documented it in detail in a previous article.&lt;/a&gt; is based on AsciiDoc files —&lt;code&gt;AGENT.adoc&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;INDEX.adoc&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;PROMPT_REPRISE.adoc&lt;/code&gt;— which load ~30 000 tokens of rules, backlog, and history at the start of each session.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And despite this documentary infrastructure, two things struck me:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The LLM forgets.&lt;/strong&gt; Even with the absolute rules at the head of each EAGER file, beyond 60,000 cumulative tokens (initial context + conversation), Kimi K2.6 has begun to propose des`Write`overwhelming on configuration files. GLM-5.1 confused a Firebase token with a placeholder to replace. The rules were written — the LLM no longer &lt;strong&gt;saw&lt;/strong&gt; them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance itself becomes a problem.&lt;/strong&gt; After implementing the Hot/Warm/Cold mechanism&lt;a href=&quot;0110_mecanisme_backup_contexte_agent_post.html&quot;&gt;Article on backup rotation.&lt;/a&gt; to avoid context explosion, my EAGER files still weighed 1414 lines&lt;a href=&quot;0111_audit_contexte_agent_post.html&quot;&gt;I documented this audit here.&lt;/a&gt; Governance — designed to protect the LLM from saturation — was saturating the LLM.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I needed an alignment mechanism that did not depend on the number of tokens in the prompt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The answer: stop aligning by text, and start aligning by the&lt;strong&gt;space&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_four_circles_of_trust_a_spatial_ontology&quot;&gt;The Four Circles of Trust: A Spatial Ontology&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My file`workspace/&lt;code&gt;(in&lt;/code&gt;~/workspace/`) is &lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt; a Git repository. It is the root of all my work — code, documentation, training, infrastructure. And it is structured into four zones that are not storage conventions, but&lt;strong&gt;concentric circles of trust&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 6.6666%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 13.3333%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 20%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 26.6666%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 33.3335%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Level&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Label&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Physical zone&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;CVS&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Visibility&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;0&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Secret garden&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;`workspace/`root&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Intimate — free thought, no commit, no publication&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Safe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;configuration/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Private Git (solo)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Secrets, tokens, vision archive. One person.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;2&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Library&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;office/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Private Git (expanded)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Pedagogical data, SPG/SPD, JSON schemas. Trust circle identified.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;4&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forges (public)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;foundry/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Public Git (Apache 2.0)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Source code, plugins, tests, technical documentation.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock note&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-note&quot; title=&quot;ℹ️&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
There is no level 3 in the table. Level 3 is a &lt;strong&gt;transitional&lt;/strong&gt; level: it&amp;#8217;s content of`office/`who has been anonymized and is ready to be published as open data. It does not have its own physical zone — it&amp;#8217;s a state of the data, not a location.
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each level answers a specific question:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where to deposit an idea that is not yet ready to be shared, even with a small circle?&lt;/strong&gt; → The secret garden. No Git. No pressure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where to store an API token so it doesn&amp;#8217;t leak?&lt;/strong&gt; → The safe`configuration/`). Physically isolated. No other repository can mistakenly reference it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where to co-build a training catalogue with a pilot OF?&lt;/strong&gt; → The library (&lt;code&gt;office/&lt;/code&gt;). Versioned, collaborative, but private.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where to industrialize an open-source Gradle plugin?&lt;/strong&gt; → Forges`foundry/`). Public, forkable, tested in CI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This ontology is&lt;strong&gt;consumable by an LLM&lt;/strong&gt;. When he reads a file in`foundry/plantuml-gradle/src/`, he implicitly knows: &quot;I am in circle 4 — public code, mandatory tests, no secrets, no educational data&quot;. He does not need a prompt reminding him of that.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_secret_garden_the_space_outside_cvs&quot;&gt;The Secret Garden: The Space Outside CVS&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is the most important concept — and the most counterintuitive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The root`workspace/&lt;code&gt;does not have&lt;/code&gt;.git/&lt;code&gt;. The documents that live there (`WORKSPACE_VISION.adoc&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;WORKSPACE_AS_PRODUCT.adoc&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;WORKSPACE_ORGANIZATION.adoc&lt;/code&gt;— and the one you are reading right now, which stems from it) are not intended to be versioned, shared, or even reread by anyone other than me. These are&lt;strong&gt;germinating thoughts&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock important&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-important&quot; title=&quot;❗&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The secret garden is &lt;strong&gt;out-of-CVS&lt;/strong&gt; by nature. The lack of versioning is the condition of freedom of thought. One does not write there to be read — one writes there to clarify one&amp;#8217;s own vision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But this freedom has a cost: a`rm`accidentally, and it&amp;#8217;s months of strategic thinking that disappear. The solution is not to version the garden (that would destroy it) — it&amp;#8217;s to&lt;strong&gt;mirror&lt;/strong&gt;in the smallest circle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect3&quot;&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&quot;_the_gitignore_as_configuration_of_governance&quot;&gt;The &lt;code&gt;.gitignore&lt;/code&gt; as Configuration of Governance&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the root of`workspace/&lt;code&gt;, a file&lt;/code&gt;.gitignore`minimal declares the&lt;strong&gt;historization policy&lt;/strong&gt;some files of the secret garden:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;.goosehints
.goose&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ce &lt;code&gt;.gitignore`does not have a classic Git function (there is no&lt;/code&gt;.git/`at the root). It acts as a&lt;strong&gt;governance configuration file&lt;/strong&gt;that answers a specific question: &lt;strong&gt;which artifacts of the secret garden deserve to be historicized, and which are purely transient?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The files listed in`.gitignore`—&lt;code&gt;.goosehints&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;.goose&lt;/code&gt;— are ephemeral artifacts generated by the agents. No strategic value. No archiving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The files`.adoc`of the root —&lt;code&gt;WORKSPACE_VISION.adoc&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;WORKSPACE_ORGANIZATION.adoc&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;WORKSPACE_AS_PRODUCT.adoc&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;WHAT_THE_GAMES_BEEN_MISSING.adoc&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;depots_implementes_strategie.adoc&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;synthese-LLMs-long-contexte.adoc&lt;/code&gt;— are not&lt;strong&gt;not&lt;/strong&gt;in the`.gitignore`. They are the artifacts to be historicized.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Le `.gitignore`is the&lt;strong&gt;governance framework&lt;/strong&gt;: everything not listed there is a candidate for the snapshot. And the LLM, by reading this file, knows exactly what should be archived and what can be ignored — without needing to be reminded in a prompt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect3&quot;&gt;
&lt;h4 id=&quot;_the_snapshot_mechanism&quot;&gt;The Snapshot Mechanism&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I have created`configuration/vision-archive/&lt;code&gt;: dated snapshots of all the&lt;/code&gt;.adoc`from the root, committed in the private repository`configuration/`. Each brainstorming session produces a snapshot:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;DATE=$(date +%Y-%m-%d)
mkdir -p /home/cheroliv/workspace/configuration/vision-archive/$DATE
cp /home/cheroliv/workspace/*.adoc /home/cheroliv/workspace/configuration/vision-archive/$DATE/
cd /home/cheroliv/workspace/configuration &amp;amp;&amp;amp; git add vision-archive/ &amp;amp;&amp;amp; \
  git commit -m &quot;vision-archive: snapshot $DATE&quot;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The procedure is triggered at the end of the session by the LLM itself, which executes this overall routing task. Each snapshot captures the full state of strategic thinking at a given moment T.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Git history of`configuration/`becomes the&lt;strong&gt;biography of my strategic thought&lt;/strong&gt;. I can do a`git log&amp;#8201;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8201;vision-archive/`and see the evolution of my vision, session by session, date by date.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Real example of history after a workday:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;$ git -C configuration log --oneline -- vision-archive/
1089d1b vision-archive: fin de session finale 2026-05-03
6b21eaf vision-archive: fin de session 2026-05-03-1300
1690f82 vision-archive: post-article 2026-05-03
28e6593 vision-archive: post-migration 2026-05-03
3707b78 vision-archive: snapshot 2026-05-03 — jardin secret initial&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Five snapshots in one day. Each is a restore point. Each is a milestone in the genesis of the strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The dossier`configuration/vision-archive/latest/`contains permanently a&lt;strong&gt;working copy&lt;/strong&gt;of the latest snapshot, serving as a quick reference without having to navigate the Git history.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And for the LLM, it&amp;#8217;s a&lt;strong&gt;oracle of coherence&lt;/strong&gt;when he observes a contradiction between the current implementation and the archived vision at an earlier date, he can report it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_vault_configuration_as_spring_cloud_config&quot;&gt;The Vault: &lt;code&gt;configuration/&lt;/code&gt; as Spring Cloud Config&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;`configuration/`It does not contain only the archive of vision. Its primary — and future — function is to be a&lt;strong&gt;server Spring Cloud Config&lt;/strong&gt;. All secrets, tokens, credentials, and infrastructure descriptors live here, in a private Git repository accessible only to the owner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Why a separate repository rather than a file`.env`in each project?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accidental push of a secret&lt;/strong&gt;: impossible. Secrets are in a private repository that public projects cannot mistakenly reference.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audit&lt;/strong&gt;: Git history provides the trail of every configuration change. Who changed what, when, with which SHA hash.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rollback&lt;/strong&gt;:`git revert`on a broken configuration. Snapshot, without manual backup.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_library_office_as_consumable_data&quot;&gt;The Library : &lt;code&gt;office/&lt;/code&gt; as Consumable Data&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;`office/`is the documentary counterpart of the development work. It contains the blog posts, the technical specifications, the training materials (38 course directories FPA, SPG/SPD, JSON schemas, Bloom/Harrow/Krathwohl taxonomies) — everything that constitutes the&lt;strong&gt;pedagogical material&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But`office/`is not just a docs drawer. It&amp;#8217;s a&lt;strong&gt;structured data source&lt;/strong&gt;that the Gradle plugins of`foundry/`They consume. A blog post in`office/`is an entry that a plugin will convert to HTML. An SPG AsciiDoc in`office/metiers/FPA/`is an artifact that an orchestrator will parse to generate slides, quizzes, and video capsules.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Et le `build.gradle.kts`at the root of`office/`is not business code — it&amp;#8217;s a&lt;strong&gt;plugin ecosystem consumption script&lt;/strong&gt;. He says: &quot;here are the Gradle plugins I use, here is the context of my workspace&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_forges_foundry_as_implementation&quot;&gt;The Forges: &lt;code&gt;foundry/&lt;/code&gt; as Implementation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;foundry/`contains the&lt;strong&gt;industrialized code&lt;/strong&gt;. 54 Git repositories, of which 7 are currently governed by&lt;/code&gt;.agents/`. This is where the vision becomes executable — Gradle plugins, CI/CD, JUnit5 + Cucumber tests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The relationship with`office/`is bidirectional:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;office/&lt;/code&gt;→`foundry/`Pedagogical data are the raw material that plugins consume.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;foundry/&lt;/code&gt;→&lt;code&gt;office/&lt;/code&gt;: the plugins produce data that enriches`office/` — le `graph.json`of graphify-gradle, compiled slider decks, build reports&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_procontra_spatial_alignment_vs_prompt_alignment&quot;&gt;Pro/Contra: Spatial Alignment vs Prompt Alignment&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;#8217;s compare the two approaches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_classic_approach_alignment_via_pre_prompt&quot;&gt;Classic Approach: Alignment via Pre-Prompt&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 20%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 80%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;(Note: Since no actual French text was provided for translation—only the instruction text in English—there is nothing to translate. Per strict adherence to the output requirements, only the translated content should be emitted, which in this case is an empty string.)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;❌ against&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Simple to implement. A block of text in the system prompt.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fragile to long context&lt;/strong&gt; : the rule is drowned after 80K tokens.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Works for general rules (tone, format).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unverifiable&lt;/strong&gt; : nothing prevents the LLM from violating the rule.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;No need to rethink the project&amp;#8217;s architecture.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Non-transferable&lt;/strong&gt; : each repo redeclares the rules.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purely declarative&lt;/strong&gt;: the LLM knows it &lt;strong&gt;should&lt;/strong&gt;, but nothing stops it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_this_approach_alignment_via_spatial_ontology&quot;&gt;This Approach: Alignment via Spatial Ontology&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 20%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 80%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;�✅ Pro&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;against&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resilient to long context&lt;/strong&gt;: the rule is in the file path, not in a distant prompt.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial infrastructure cost&lt;/strong&gt;: structuring the workspace into circles takes time.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mechanically verifiable&lt;/strong&gt; : a secret in`foundry/&lt;code&gt;is detectable by`git check-ignore&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requires discipline&lt;/strong&gt; : a new contributor must understand the circles.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transferable&lt;/strong&gt;: a`AGENT.adoc`standard exposes the circles to any new project.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Covers only spatial constraints&lt;/strong&gt; — the code style remains in the prompt.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security by design&lt;/strong&gt; : a`git push`since`foundry/&lt;code&gt;cannot expose`configuration/&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consumable by non-LLM agents&lt;/strong&gt; : a Gradle orchestrator can route according to the circle.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The main gain is not defensive (security, visibility) — it is&lt;strong&gt;creative&lt;/strong&gt;. When the LLM works in a space structured by an ontology, it can do what no prompt allows it: &lt;strong&gt;observe the delta&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_relational_algebra_of_the_workspace_and_the_observable_delta&quot;&gt;The Relational Algebra of the Workspace and the Observable Delta&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When the LLM traverses`foundry/&lt;code&gt;, it has a&lt;strong&gt;structured data lattice&lt;/strong&gt;: nodes (plugins, files, tests, dependencies), typed edges (`import&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;depends_on&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;generates&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;tests&lt;/code&gt;), composition and order relations (`training-gradle`extracts the repository`slider-gradle`generates the slides →`capsule-gradle`edit the video)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This algebra is not written anywhere in plain — but it is &lt;strong&gt;observable&lt;/strong&gt;. Each`build.gradle.kts`exposes dependencies. Each`INDEX.adoc`exposes cross-references.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The LLM observes this algebra and detects the&lt;strong&gt;delta&lt;/strong&gt;The gap between what the system already knows how to produce and what the vision describes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From this delta, it can define some&lt;strong&gt;business expert mappings&lt;/strong&gt;— CDA (Application Designer/Developer, Kotlin/Gradle/JHipster) and FPA (Professional Adult Trainer, Pedagogy/Qualiopi/Bloom) — and identify what is missing for each expert.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;Expert CDA (Kotlin/Gradle/JHipster)
  ├── Plugins : jhipster-gradle-plugins, plantuml-gradle,
  │   codebase-gradle
  ├── Delta : pas encore de SPG CDA formalisé,
  │   pas de fine-tuning expert CDA

Expert FPA (Pédagogie/Qualiopi/Bloom)
  ├── Plugins : training-gradle, slider-gradle,
  │   school-backoffice/forms, capsule-gradle
  ├── Matériel : 38 modules cours, SPG/SPD, taxonomies
  └── Delta : parser AsciiDoc→JSON à créer,
      orchestrateur à coder&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The LLM doesn&amp;#8217;t need to be told what to do. The delta emerges from the structure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_composite_context_vector_rag_pgvector_graphify&quot;&gt;The Composite Context Vector: RAG + pgvector + Graphify&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Relational algebra is not a theoretical construct. It is &lt;strong&gt;materialized&lt;/strong&gt; by three components that form a&lt;strong&gt;composite context vector&lt;/strong&gt;for the LLM.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_component_1_langchain4j_rag_postgresql_pgvector&quot;&gt;Component 1 — LangChain4j RAG + PostgreSQL pgvector&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I already have LangChain4j in production in two plugins :`slider-gradle`(4 providers LLM) and`plantuml-gradle`(7 providers). The ONNX embeddings (AllMiniLmL6V2) index the data of`office/`and the source code of`foundry/`in PostgreSQL + pgvector.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This RAG operates on two dimensions:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dimension data&lt;/strong&gt;: the documents`office/`(SPG, articles, formations, JSON schemas)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dimension code&lt;/strong&gt; : the codebases`foundry/`(sources Kotlin, tests Cucumber, AGENT.adoc)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The intersection covers both the &lt;strong&gt;what&lt;/strong&gt; (the business domain) and the &lt;strong&gt;how&lt;/strong&gt; (the implementation).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_component_2_knowledge_graph_graphify&quot;&gt;Component 2 — Knowledge Graph Graphify&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphify is integrated into`plantuml-gradle`(109 tests, 380/380 PASS) and produces a`graph.json`— a structured knowledge graph with nodes, edges, and automatically detected communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Unlike RAG which operates by vector similarity (fuzzy), the knowledge graph operates by&lt;strong&gt;exact relations&lt;/strong&gt;(deterministic)`graphify query`for the semantic questions (~50 tokens),`graphify path`to navigate,`graphify explain`to explain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_component_3_incremental_graphify_sparse_aggregable_consumable&quot;&gt;Component 3 — Incremental Graphify : Sparse, Aggregable, Consumable&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is the key architectural decision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphify must not live in a single repository. It must live in a manner&lt;strong&gt;scattered&lt;/strong&gt;in each plugin:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Each plugin&lt;/strong&gt; bundles a Gradle task`updateKnowledgeGraph`who calls Graphify&lt;strong&gt;on its own scope&lt;/strong&gt;and produces a`graph.json`local.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The build script of`office/&lt;code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; consumes`graphify-gradle`with`rootDir = /home/cheroliv/workspace`and produces a`graph.json&lt;/code&gt; &lt;strong&gt;global&lt;/strong&gt;that aggregates the local graphs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The RAG of each plugin&lt;/strong&gt; injects the`graph.json`global as&lt;strong&gt;context filter&lt;/strong&gt;for the LLM requests.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;TÂCHE GRADLE (dans chaque plugin)
    ↓
graphify → graph.json (scope local)
    ↓
office/build.gradle.kts → graph.json (scope global)
    ↓
RAG pgvector (dans slider, plantuml, codebase...)
    ↓  ← injection du graph.json comme filtre
LLM (deepseek-v4-pro)
    ↓  ← observation algèbre relationnelle
    ↓  ← détection delta vs cartographies experts
PRIORISATION → prochaine tâche&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Result: the LLM is not searching in a void — it is navigating a space structured by the knowledge graph. A query on &quot;génère un diagramme&quot; knows how to reach the relevant nodes of the graph.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_automatic_gdpr_classification_the_llm_as_router&quot;&gt;Automatic GDPR Classification: the LLM as Router&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The spatial ontology does not merely align the LLM — it gives it a&lt;strong&gt;GDPR classification grid&lt;/strong&gt;to route each data item to its legitimate zone&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 12.5%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 37.5%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 25%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 25%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Criterion&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;LLM detection&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Action&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Maximum level&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Personal data (name, email, IP)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Pattern`@`, IP, proper nouns&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Anonymize →`[OF_PILOTE]`or level 2 router&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;2&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Token / Secret / Credential&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;pattern`sk-&amp;#8230;&amp;#8203;&lt;code&gt;, `ghp_&amp;#8230;&amp;#8203;&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;ya29&amp;#8230;&amp;#8203;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Router →&lt;code&gt;configuration/&lt;/code&gt;. Reference by`${VAR}`in the code.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;internal URL&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Contains`localhost`, private IP&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Anonymize →&lt;code&gt;${API_URL}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;2&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Pedagogical data (SPG, course)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Structure Bloom/Qualiopi&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Router →&lt;code&gt;office/&lt;/code&gt;(level 2). Double version if export.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;3&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Source code / test&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Extension`.kt`, &lt;code&gt;.kts`in`foundry/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Router →&lt;code&gt;foundry/&lt;/code&gt;. Check for absence of secrets.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;4&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the end of the session, the LLM executes a&lt;strong&gt;global task&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reading of`.gitignore`root to identify ephemeral artifacts (to exclude from the snapshot) vs strategic artifacts (to be historicized)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inventory of all files`.adoc`of the root`workspace/`&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Filtering: exclusion of files listed in`.gitignore`, inclusion of all the others&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Copy in`configuration/vision-archive/$DATE/&lt;code&gt;and update of the symlink`latest/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Commit in the repository`configuration/`with a structured message&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Automatic GDPR classification of each modified file (all circles)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Routing: data`office/&lt;code&gt;→ private commit, code`foundry/&lt;/code&gt;→&lt;code&gt;./gradlew check&lt;/code&gt;, configuration → commit&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Structured report with GDPR alerts and archiving confirmation&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Le `.gitignore`root is not a Git configuration file — it&amp;#8217;s a&lt;strong&gt;historization governance file&lt;/strong&gt;. It defines the schema that the LLM consumes to decide which files from the secret garden go into the strategic biography and which are disposable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The LLM is no longer just a text generator. It is the&lt;strong&gt;information manager&lt;/strong&gt;of the ecosystem — producer, classifier, router.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_roadmap_from_asciidoc_to_langgraph4j&quot;&gt;Roadmap: from AsciiDoc to LangGraph4j&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, this governance is &lt;strong&gt;deterministic&lt;/strong&gt;: the LLM applies a procedure described in AsciiDoc files. It is the&lt;strong&gt;phase 1&lt;/strong&gt;— prompt engineering with LLM memory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;La &lt;strong&gt;phase 2&lt;/strong&gt;will extract each step of the procedure into a&lt;strong&gt;typed Gradle task&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;./gradlew endSessionWorkspace    → snapshot vision-archive
./gradlew endSessionProject      → archive .agents/
./gradlew endSessionReport       → rapport multi-zones&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;La &lt;strong&gt;phase 3&lt;/strong&gt;will model the end-of-session process as a&lt;strong&gt;state graph&lt;/strong&gt;withhttps://github.com/langgraph4j/langgraph4j[LangGraph4j]:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;[Start] → [Inventaire fichiers modifiés]
       → [Classification RGPD] (nœud ONNX)
       → [Branchement par cercle]
            ├→ cercle 0 → snapshot → commit
            ├→ cercle 2 → anonymisation → commit
            ├→ cercle 4 → archive → commit
            └→ cercle 1 → commit configuration/
       → [Rapport] → [End]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This graph will be versioned in CI/CD, executed by Gradle, configured via the GitHub Secrets of the plugins. The LLM will no longer have to decide on routing — the graph will do it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_what_this_architecture_solves_and_what_it_does_not_solve&quot;&gt;What This Architecture Solves (and what it does not Solve)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock caution&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-caution&quot; title=&quot;🔒&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The spatial ontology does not cover everything. Code style conventions, naming, architectural design choices—all of that remains in the prompt. What the spatial ontology solves is the&lt;strong&gt;security and visibility layer&lt;/strong&gt;: where each byte must live, and who can see it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here is what it concretely brings:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No`git push`accidental of a secret&lt;/strong&gt;: the secrets are in`configuration/&lt;code&gt;(circle 1). Public projects are in`foundry/&lt;/code&gt;(circle 4). No path crosses both.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No business code in the data&lt;/strong&gt; :`office/&lt;code&gt;contains some&lt;/code&gt;.adoc`, some YAML, JSON schemas — but no`.kt`. Le `build.gradle.kts`who lives there is a consumption script, not business code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No strategic thinking exposed&lt;/strong&gt; : the vision documents live in the secret garden (root outside CVS). The snapshots are in`configuration/`(private vault). Nobody, even in an expanded circle of trust, reads the genesis of the strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Auto-prioritization&lt;/strong&gt; : the LLM observes the delta between relational algebra (what exists) and expert mappings (what is necessary). The next development task emerges from this delta.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_conclusion_architecture_as_discourse&quot;&gt;Conclusion: Architecture as Discourse&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I don&amp;#8217;t put a political manifesto in the footer of my site. I don&amp;#8217;t put ethical rules in my prompts. Alignment is not in the text — it is in the&lt;strong&gt;file system&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When an LLM works in this space, it cannot leak a secret (the path prevents it). It cannot confuse a teaching datum with source code (the physical zone is different). It cannot forget a security rule at 80,000 tokens — because the rule is not in the prompt, it is in the`workspace/` → &lt;code&gt;configuration/&lt;/code&gt;→&lt;code&gt;office/&lt;/code&gt;→`foundry/`that each file reading is reactive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It&amp;#8217;s the principle of &lt;strong&gt;secure by design&lt;/strong&gt; applied to agent alignment: do not ask the LLM to remember the rules. Make the architecture such that error is structurally impossible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And by the way, that gives the LLM something no prompt can give it: the ability to&lt;strong&gt;perceive&lt;/strong&gt;where it is, what exists, what is missing — and deduce what it must do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_references&quot;&gt;References&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
