&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;preamble&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;reading time : 12 minutes&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For months, the contact form on this site ran on a JavaScript mock — an 85% success promise, a fake Firestore, zero data stored. The initial plan had a Supabase backend with Google Apps Script for email notifications. Abandoned. Today, I tell the story of migrating to Firebase Firestore: project creation, security rules, JS rewriting, cleaning up dead Supabase code. And why this choice says something larger about development philosophy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;dlist&quot;&gt;
&lt;dl&gt;
&lt;dt class=&quot;hdlist1&quot;&gt;toc&lt;/dt&gt;
&lt;dd&gt;
&lt;p&gt;[]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/dd&gt;
&lt;/dl&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_scene_a_form_that_stores_nothing&quot;&gt;The scene: a form that stores nothing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This site is generated by JBake, my Gradle plugin`bakery`. It is 100% static — no backend, no database. Except that I have a contact form. The page`contact.html`it exists, the HTML is ready (fields name, email, phone, subject, message, HTML5 validation, anti-spam honeypot), the Bootstrap styles are in place. Visually, everything is perfect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Except that at submission, nothing happens.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-javascript hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;javascript&quot;&gt;const firebaseMock = new Promise((resolve, reject) =&amp;gt; {
    setTimeout(() =&amp;gt; {
        if (Math.random() &amp;lt; 0.85) {
            resolve({ status: 201, message: &#39;Message stored in Firestore.&#39; });
        } else {
            reject({ status: 500, message: &#39;Firestore write failed.&#39; });
        }
    }, 1500);
});&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A mock. A promise that pretends. The user sees a spinner, then a message « Message sent successfully! ». But the data goes into the void. No message is stored anywhere.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The situation is worse than a broken form — it&amp;#8217;s a form that lies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_supabase_heritage&quot;&gt;Supabase heritage&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The initial plan, documented in`content/draft/integration_formulaire_contact_supabase.adoc`, expected :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A Supabase database with table`contacts`and Row Level Security&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;an RPC`handle_contact_form`server side&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A SQL trigger calling a Google Apps Script webhook&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Google Apps Script that sends a Gmail notification email&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The corresponding JavaScript code still exists in`script.js`. There is a class`SupabaseManager`that initializes a Supabase client with global variables`SUPABASE_URL` et &lt;code&gt;SUPABASE_KEY&lt;/code&gt;, and a class`ContactFormHandler`who listens to the form&amp;#8217;s submit event and calls`SupabaseManager.submitContactForm()`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Problem: these global variables are no longer injected into the footer. the`&amp;lt;script src=&quot;supabase-js&quot;&amp;gt;`has been removed. The code calls`supabase.createClient()`on a variable`supabase`that no longer exists. So:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;console.error : &#39;Supabase client library (supabase-js) is not loaded.&#39;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not only are the data not stored, but the submission code is dead.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_phantom_double_submission&quot;&gt;The phantom double submission&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To make matters worse, there is a&lt;strong&gt;silent competition&lt;/strong&gt;between two handlers on the same form :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;`contact.js`listen to the submit, call the mock Firebase&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;script.js&lt;/code&gt;— via`ContactFormHandler`— also listen to the submit, call`SupabaseManager`&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Both do`event.preventDefault() + event.stopPropagation()&lt;code&gt;. As`contact.js`is loaded first in`footer.thyme&lt;/code&gt;, its handler is attached first. It blocks propagation.`ContactFormHandler`will never be triggered.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It&amp;#8217;s not even an active bug — it&amp;#8217;s a zombie. Code that never gets a chance to run.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;diag-before&quot; class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 6) ]

