&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_next_steps_backlog&quot;&gt;Next steps (backlog)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Notification email&lt;/strong&gt;: A Cloud Function`onCreate`on`contact_messages`who sends an email via SendGrid. The form stores, but I am not notified. Medium priority — the messages are visible in the Firebase console.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rate limiting client-side&lt;/strong&gt;: Add a localStorage timestamp to prevent multiple submissions in rapid succession. The honeypot blocks naive bots, a rate limiter would block slightly more clever bots.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tests&lt;/strong&gt;: A Playwright test that submits the form and verifies that the document appears in Firestore. For now, I&amp;#8217;m testing manually via`./gradlew serve`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
