&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The technical report explicitly states: DSA is &lt;em&gt;&quot;lossless by construction&quot;&lt;/em&gt; — unlike alternatives such as SWA (pattern search), Gated DeltaNet, or SimpleGDN, which lose up to 5.69 points on RULER@128K.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_sessions_11_13_solid_but_frustrating&quot;&gt;Sessions 11-13: solid but frustrating&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GLM-5.1 holds distance better. During session 11 (~60K tokens), it remains coherent. It produces a`SnapshotManager`functional with correct management of the four anonymizers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But latency is a problem. DSA reasoning phases are heavier than pure MLA — the indexer must rescan the history at each step. A response that took 8 seconds with Kimi takes 15 with GLM. In a 30‑message session, it’s felt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And then there are the subtle errors. GLM doesn&amp;#8217;t hallucinate like Kimi — but it makes &lt;strong&gt;naming&lt;/strong&gt; errors. He calls`toAnonymizedYaml()&lt;code&gt;the method that should be called`anonymize()&lt;/code&gt;. It reverses`loadReadmeConfiguration()` et &lt;code&gt;loadCodebaseConfiguration()`in the`renderFileSection()&lt;/code&gt;. These are not hallucinations, they are superficial confusions — but in production, a superficial confusion can break a build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I held three sessions with GLM. It is better than Kimi, without a doubt. But three sessions of manual correction on naming details are exhausting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_round_3_deepseek_v4_pro_the_war_machine&quot;&gt;Round 3 : DeepSeek-V4-Pro — The War Machine&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DeepSeek-V4-Pro arrives with the most ambitious architecture of the three: a hybrid system that combines two complementary attention mechanisms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_architecture_csa_hca_the_double_net&quot;&gt;Architecture: CSA + HCA, the double net&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;diag-csa-hca&quot; class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 9) ]

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam wrapWidth 180

title DeepSeek-V4-Pro — Hybrid CSA + HCA Architecture
left to right direction

rectangle &quot;KV Cache
