&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 7.1428%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 7.1428%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 7.1428%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 7.1428%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 7.1428%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 7.1428%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 7.1428%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 7.1428%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 7.1428%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 7.1428%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 7.1428%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 7.1428%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 7.1428%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 7.1436%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Component&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Target version&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Gradle&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;9.4.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Java&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;21.0.11-tem (Eclipse Temurin)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;JHipster&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;8.x (framework`tech.jhipster:jhipster-framework:8.11.0`)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Spring Boot&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;3.4.5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Kotlin&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;2.3.0&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Docker Engine&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;29.4.1 (API 1.54)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Changing the Java version goes through SDKMAN :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;sdk use java 21.0.11-tem&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;First launch:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ ./gradlew build --no-daemon

FAILURE: Build failed with an exception.

* Where:
Build file &#39;/home/.../edster/build.gradle&#39; line: 18

* What went wrong:
An exception occurred applying plugin request [id: &#39;jhipster.cucumber-conventions&#39;]
&amp;gt; Failed to apply plugin &#39;jhipster.cucumber-conventions&#39;.
   &amp;gt; Could not create task &#39;:cucumberTest&#39;.
      &amp;gt; Could not create task &#39;:consoleLauncherTest&#39;.
         &amp;gt; Could not set unknown property &#39;reportsDir&#39; for task &#39;:consoleLauncherTest&#39;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don&amp;#8217;t even get off loading the build script. The problem is in`buildSrc/src/main/groovy/jhipster.cucumber-conventions.gradle`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_error_1_the_phantom_variable_reportsdir&quot;&gt;Error 1: the phantom variable `reportsDir&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The script`jhipster.cucumber-conventions.gradle`contains :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-groovy hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;groovy&quot;&gt;tasks.register(&#39;consoleLauncherTest&#39;, JavaExec) {
    dependsOn(testClasses)
    String cucumberReportsDir = file(&quot;$buildDir/reports/tests&quot;)
    outputs.dir(reportsDir)           // &amp;lt;-- reportsDir n&#39;existe PAS
    classpath = sourceSets[&quot;test&quot;].runtimeClasspath
    main = &quot;org.junit.platform.console.ConsoleLauncher&quot;
    // ...
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The defined variable is`cucumberReportsDir`. The used one is`reportsDir`-- which is not defined anywhere.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Correction&lt;/strong&gt;:`outputs.dir(cucumberReportsDir)`&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_error_2_main_no_longer_exists_in_gradle_9&quot;&gt;Error 2: &lt;code&gt;main = &quot;&amp;#8230;&amp;#8203;&quot;&lt;/code&gt; no longer exists in Gradle 9&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Immediate follow-up:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;Could not set unknown property &#39;main&#39; for task &#39;:consoleLauncherTest&#39; of type org.gradle.api.tasks.JavaExec.&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gradle 9 removes the property`main`for the benefit of`mainClass`on the tasks`JavaExec`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Correction&lt;/strong&gt; : &lt;code&gt;mainClass = &quot;org.junit.platform.console.ConsoleLauncher&quot;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_error_3_sourcecompatibility_is_no_longer_a_project_property&quot;&gt;Error 3: &lt;code&gt;sourceCompatibility&lt;/code&gt; is no longer a project property&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;New error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;Could not set unknown property &#39;sourceCompatibility&#39; for root project &#39;edster&#39; of type org.gradle.api.Project.&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The root script had:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-groovy hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;groovy&quot;&gt;sourceCompatibility=17
targetCompatibility=17&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gradle 9 removes these properties at the root level. They must live in a block`java`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Correction&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-groovy hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;groovy&quot;&gt;java {
    sourceCompatibility = JavaVersion.VERSION_21
    targetCompatibility = JavaVersion.VERSION_21
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_error_4_the_three_operand_groovy_assertion&quot;&gt;Error 4: the three-operand Groovy assertion&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The old script contained:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-groovy hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;groovy&quot;&gt;assert System.properties[&quot;java.specification.version&quot;] == &quot;17&quot; || &quot;21&quot; || &quot;24&quot;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In Groovy`&quot;21&quot;` et &lt;code&gt;&quot;24&quot;`are truthy strings. The expression resolves to&lt;/code&gt;(&amp;#8230;&amp;#8203; == &quot;17&quot;) || true || true`, which is always true&amp;#8201;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8201;but the syntax is invalid for the strict assertion desired.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Correction&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-groovy hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;groovy&quot;&gt;assert System.properties[&quot;java.specification.version&quot;] in [&quot;17&quot;, &quot;21&quot;, &quot;23&quot;, &quot;24&quot;]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_error_5_the_implicit_dependency_compilekotlin_openapigenerate&quot;&gt;Error 5: the implicit dependency &lt;code&gt;compileKotlin&lt;/code&gt; → `openApiGenerate&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The build is progressing. Kotlin compilation succeeded. Then :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;Task &#39;:compileKotlin&#39; uses this output of task &#39;:openApiGenerate&#39;
without declaring an explicit or implicit dependency.&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Gradle 9 refuses implicit dependencies between tasks. Since`compileKotlin`reads the sources generated by`openApiGenerate`, you must declare the link.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Correction&lt;/strong&gt;in`build.gradle`:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-groovy hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;groovy&quot;&gt;afterEvaluate {
    tasks.named(&quot;compileKotlin&quot;).configure {
        dependsOn(tasks.named(&quot;openApiGenerate&quot;))
    }
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Le `afterEvaluate`is necessary because`openApiGenerate`is an extension (OpenAPI Generator plugin) and not a task directly accessible during the configuration phase.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_error_6_generategitproperties_breaks_on_filteroutputstream_write&quot;&gt;Error 6: &lt;code&gt;generateGitProperties&lt;/code&gt; breaks on `FilterOutputStream.write()&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Java compilation passes. Resources are processed. Then:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;&amp;gt; Task :generateGitProperties FAILED

No signature of method: java.io.FilterOutputStream.write() is applicable for argument types: (Integer) values: [103]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The plugin`gradle-git-properties`version 2.5.0 is incompatible with Java 21 / Gradle 9. An internal bug attempts to call`write(int)`via Groovy on a stream that closed it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Correction&lt;/strong&gt;in`gradle.properties`:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-properties hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;properties&quot;&gt;gitPropertiesPluginVersion=2.5.7&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_finally_testcontainers_steps_onto_the_stage&quot;&gt;Finally: Testcontainers steps onto the stage&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Until now, it was pure &quot;build script debugging&quot;. Every error was a Gradle 9 or Java 21 incompatibility in the build scripts. After the six fixes above, the`./gradlew assemble`passes successfully.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But`./gradlew build`It also runs the tests, and the Cucumber tests use Testcontainers to start an ephemeral PostgreSQL.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;Could not find a valid Docker environment.

EnvironmentAndSystemPropertyClientProviderStrategy: failed with exception BadRequestException
(Status 400: {&quot;message&quot;:&quot;client version 1.32 is too old. Minimum supported API version is 1.40&quot;}
UnixSocketClientProviderStrategy: failed with exception BadRequestException
(Status 400: {&quot;message&quot;:&quot;client version 1.32 is too old. Minimum supported API version is 1.40&quot;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Testcontainers is unable to communicate with Docker. Two different strategies (environment variables + Unix socket) fail with the same error.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;diag-docker-handshake&quot; class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 5) ]

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam handwritten false

actor &quot;Testcontainers
^^^^^
 Syntax Error? (Assumed diagram type: sequence)

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam handwritten false

actor &quot;Testcontainers
1.20.6&quot; as TC
participant &quot;docker-java
3.4.1&quot; as DJ
participant &quot;Docker Engine
29.4.1&quot; as DE

TC -&amp;gt; DJ : new DockerClient()
DJ -&amp;gt; DE : GET /_ping\nUser-Agent: docker-java/3.4.1\nAPI-Version: 1.32
DE --&amp;gt; DJ : HTTP 400 Bad Request\nclient version 1.32 is too old.\nMinimum supported API version is 1.40
DJ --&amp;gt; TC : BadRequestException
TC --&amp;gt; TC : Could not find a valid\nDocker environment

note right of DE
  Docker Engine 29.x impose
  API minimum = 1.40
  (défaut ancien : 1.24)
end note

note left of DJ
  docker-java 3.4.1 envoie
  hardcoded API version 1.32
  dans l&#39;en-tête HTTP
end note

@enduml&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_phase_1_the_docker_java_track&quot;&gt;Phase 1: the docker-java track&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;First reflex: the Java Docker client used by Testcontainers sends the API version`1.32`in its HTTP handshake, but Docker Engine 29.4.1 requires a minimum of`1.40`. The problem is at the client level, not the daemon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Checking the docker-java version resolved by Testcontainers 1.20.6 :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ ./gradlew dependencies --configuration testRuntimeClasspath | grep docker-java

+--- com.github.docker-java:docker-java-api:3.4.1
+--- com.github.docker-java:docker-java-transport:3.4.1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;docker-java 3.4.1, dating from Testcontainers 1.20.6. The latest public version of docker-java is 3.5.1. Let&amp;#8217;s try to force the version upgrade via`resolutionStrategy`in the block`configurations` de &lt;code&gt;build.gradle&lt;/code&gt;(Empty output)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-groovy hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;groovy&quot;&gt;configurations {
    all {
        resolutionStrategy.eachDependency { details -&amp;gt;
            if (details.requested.group == &quot;com.github.docker-java&quot;
                &amp;amp;&amp;amp; details.requested.name.startsWith(&quot;docker-java&quot;)) {
                details.useVersion(&quot;3.5.1&quot;)
            }
        }
    }
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Restarting build. Same error:`client version 1.32 is too old`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Checking Gradle cache: the JARs have indeed been re-downloaded, but the error persists. docker-java 3.5.1 still sends`1.32`. This version is therefore NOT sufficient for Docker Engine 29.4.1.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purification action&lt;/strong&gt;: completely clear the Gradle cache, just to be sure :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;rm -rf ~/.gradle/caches
rm -rf /path/to/project/.gradle&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Full restart after purge. Same error.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_phase_2_web_search_and_github_breadcrumb&quot;&gt;Phase 2: web search and GitHub breadcrumb&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;docker-java 3.5.1 is insufficient. All that remains is to check if anyone has encountered this exact problem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Targeted search on testcontainers-java and docker-java issues:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;site:github.com/testcontainers &quot;client version 1.32 is too old&quot;
site:github.com/docker-java &quot;client version 1.32&quot; Docker Engine 29&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;First immediate results:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/testcontainers/testcontainers-java/issues/11210&quot;&gt;testcontainers-java#11210&lt;/a&gt;—&lt;code&gt;[Bug]: client version 1.32 is too old. Minimum supported API version is 1.44&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/testcontainers/testcontainers-java/issues/11212&quot;&gt;testcontainers-java#11212&lt;/a&gt;—&lt;code&gt;[Bug]: Docker 29.0.0 could not find a valid Docker environment&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/testcontainers/testcontainers-java/issues/11491&quot;&gt;testcontainers-java#11491&lt;/a&gt;—&lt;code&gt;[Bug]: Incompatibility in Ubuntu Github runners with Docker Engine 29.1.*&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The breadcrumb is clear: Docker Engine 29.x has raised its minimum API version to`1.24`(old defect) to`1.40`. Testcontainers 1.20.x uses docker-java 3.4.x which negotiates the API version by sending`1.32`. The daemon politely but firmly refuses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In issue #11491, a maintainer replies:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;lt;/think&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This response contains&lt;strong&gt;two critical pieces of information&lt;/strong&gt; :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Testcontainers 2.0.3+ solves the problem&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The modules have been&lt;strong&gt;renamed with the prefix `testcontainers-&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_phase_3_the_trap_of_renamed_artifacts&quot;&gt;Phase 3: the trap of renamed artifacts&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Renaming is brutal. In Testcontainers 2.x, none of the old names work under that name any longer:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 10%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 10%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 10%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 10%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 10%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 10%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 10%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 10%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 10%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 10%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Old name (1.x)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;New name (2.x)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;org.testcontainers:postgresql&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;org.testcontainers:testcontainers-postgresql&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;org.testcontainers:jdbc&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;org.testcontainers:testcontainers-jdbc&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;org.testcontainers:junit-jupiter&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;org.testcontainers:testcontainers-junit-jupiter&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;org.testcontainers:testcontainers&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;unchanged&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;First attempt: apply the Testcontainers 2.0.5 BOM and the new artifact names in`build.gradle`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-groovy hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;groovy&quot;&gt;dependencies {
    testImplementation platform(&quot;org.testcontainers:testcontainers-bom:2.0.5&quot;)
    testImplementation &quot;org.testcontainers:testcontainers-postgresql&quot;
    testImplementation &quot;org.testcontainers:testcontainers-jdbc&quot;
    testImplementation &quot;org.testcontainers:testcontainers-junit-jupiter&quot;
    testImplementation &quot;org.testcontainers:testcontainers&quot;
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;./gradlew build&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;FAILURE: Could not find org.testcontainers:jdbc:2.0.5.
Could not find org.testcontainers:junit-jupiter:2.0.5.&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The testcontainers-bom BOM is not enough.&lt;/strong&gt;Why? Because Spring Boot 3.4.5 exposes its own dependency management BOM (&lt;code&gt;spring-boot-dependencies&lt;/code&gt;) who&lt;strong&gt;wins&lt;/strong&gt;on the Testcontainers BOM in transitive resolution. Spring Boot sets`testcontainers` à &lt;code&gt;1.20.6&lt;/code&gt;, and therefore all artifacts that are not explicitly in the Spring Boot BOM (such as the new`testcontainers-*&lt;code&gt;) resolve to the old names`1.20.6&lt;/code&gt;-- that no longer exist in this version&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inspecting the`dependencies --configuration testRuntimeClasspath`, one finds:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;+--- org.testcontainers:testcontainers -&amp;gt; 1.20.6 (*)
|    \--- org.testcontainers:testcontainers:2.0.5 -&amp;gt; 1.20.6&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Le &lt;code&gt;&amp;#8594;`indicates the substitution : Testcontainers 2.0.5 is &lt;strong&gt;requested&lt;/strong&gt;, but Spring Boot forces`1.20.6&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;diag-bom-war&quot; class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 8) ]

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

left to right direction

component &quot;build.gradle
^^^^^
 Syntax Error? (Assumed diagram type: class)

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

left to right direction

component &quot;build.gradle
(consumer)&quot; as BG #E3F2FD {
    rectangle &quot;request
`testcontainers-bom:2.0.5&quot; as REQ
    rectangle &quot;request\n`testcontainers-postgresql&quot; as REQ2
}

component &quot;Maven Central&quot; as MC #FFF3E0

component &quot;Declarations&quot; as DEC #E8F5E9 {
    rectangle &quot;testcontainers-bom:2.0.5`
fixes 2.0.5&quot; as BOM2
    rectangle &quot;spring-boot-dependencies:3.4.5`\nsets 1.20.6&quot; as BOM1
}

component &quot;Gradle resolution&quot; as RES #FFEBEE {
    rectangle &quot;Winning version\n`testcontainers:1.20.6&quot; as WIN #EF9A9A
}

BG --&amp;gt; DEC : &quot;analyse the BOMs&quot;
BOM2 --&amp;gt; RES : &quot;propose 2.0.5&quot;
BOM1 --&amp;gt; RES : &quot;proposes 1.20.6&quot;
WIN -&amp;gt; MC : &quot;\boxed{download
testcontainers:1.20.6}&quot;

note bottom of WIN
  Spring Boot BOM prime car
  le plugin spring-boot applique
  ses dépendances de gestion
  après la résolution du consommateur
end note

@enduml&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_phase_4_force_the_resolution&quot;&gt;Phase 4: force the resolution&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The strategy becomes twofold:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Force docker-java to version 3.7.1 (tested as compatible with Docker Engine 29)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Force Testcontainers core to 2.0.5 by bypassing the Spring Boot BOM&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;diag-resolution-override&quot; class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 9) ]

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

left to right direction

component &quot;build.gradle\n(with resolutionStrategy)&quot; as BG #E8F5E9 {
    rectangle &quot;BOM Testcontainers
^^^^^
 Syntax Error? (Assumed diagram type: class)

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam handwritten false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

left to right direction

component &quot;build.gradle\n(with resolutionStrategy)&quot; as BG #E8F5E9 {
    rectangle &quot;BOM Testcontainers
`2.0.5&quot; as BOM2
    rectangle &quot;resolutionStrategy\n.eachDependency&quot; as RS #66BB6A
}

component &quot;Conflict resolved&quot; as RESOLVED #E3F2FD {
    rectangle &quot;docker-java
`3.7.1` (forced)&quot; as DJ
    rectangle &quot;testcontainers\n`2.0.5` (forced)&quot; as TC #81C784
    rectangle &quot;testcontainers-postgresql\n`2.0.5&quot; as TPG
    rectangle &quot;testcontainers-jdbc
`2.0.5&quot; as TJ
    rectangle &quot;testcontainers-junit-jupiter
`2.0.5&quot; as TJJ
}

component &quot;BOM Spring Boot\n(implicit, overridden)&quot; as BOM1 #FFEBEE

component &quot;Maven Central&quot; as MC #FFF3E0

BG --&amp;gt; RESOLVED : &quot;BOM Testcontainers 2.0.5
passes directly&quot;
RS -&amp;gt; DJ : &quot;force 3.7.1&quot;
RS -&amp;gt; TC : &quot;force 2.0.5&quot;
RESOLVED --&amp;gt; MC : &quot;download the JARs\ncompatible Docker 29&quot;
BOM1 -[#gray,dashed]-&amp;gt; RESOLVED : &quot;ignored on testcontainers\net docker-java&quot;

note bottom of RS
  Le `eachDependency` intercepte
  la résolution Gradle AVANT
  que le BOM Spring Boot ne gagne.
  C&#39;est une intervention chirurgicale.
end note

@enduml&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Final correction&lt;/strong&gt;in`build.gradle` :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-groovy hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;groovy&quot;&gt;configurations {
    all {
        resolutionStrategy.eachDependency { details -&amp;gt;
            if (details.requested.group == &quot;com.github.docker-java&quot;
                &amp;amp;&amp;amp; details.requested.name.startsWith(&quot;docker-java&quot;)) {
                details.useVersion(&quot;3.7.1&quot;)
            }
            if (details.requested.group == &quot;org.testcontainers&quot;
                &amp;amp;&amp;amp; details.requested.name == &quot;testcontainers&quot;) {
                details.useVersion(&quot;2.0.5&quot;)
            }
        }
    }
}

dependencies {
    testImplementation platform(&quot;org.testcontainers:testcontainers-bom:2.0.5&quot;)
    testImplementation &quot;org.testcontainers:testcontainers-jdbc&quot;
    testImplementation &quot;org.testcontainers:testcontainers-junit-jupiter&quot;
    testImplementation &quot;org.testcontainers:testcontainers-postgresql&quot;
    testImplementation &quot;org.testcontainers:testcontainers&quot;
    // ... autres dépendances Spring Boot
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Le `resolutionStrategy.eachDependency`is the only way to bypass the BOM`spring-boot-dependencies`managed by the Spring Boot plugin. The equality test on`details.requested.name == &quot;testcontainers&quot;`is intentionally restrictive : we only force the core module. The modules`testcontainers-*`That follow the Testcontainers 2.0.5 BOM we explicitly declared.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_result_final&quot;&gt;Result final&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ ./gradlew build --no-daemon

&amp;gt; Task :consoleLauncherTest
[2 containers found]
[2 containers started]
[2 containers successful]

BUILD SUCCESSFUL in 1m 16s&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Testcontainers 2.0.5 + docker-java 3.7.1 finally manage to create their PostgreSQL containers via Docker Engine 29.4.1. The final business error (HTTP 500 on the Cucumber test) is a purely application problem completely independent of the build script.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_summary_table_of_corrections&quot;&gt;Summary table of corrections&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 25%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 25%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 25%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 25%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;#&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;File&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;Problem&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;Correction&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;buildSrc/src/main/groovy/jhipster.cucumber-conventions.gradle&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Variable`reportsDir`nonexistent&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;outputs.dir(cucumberReportsDir)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;2&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;buildSrc/src/main/groovy/jhipster.cucumber-conventions.gradle&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;`main`deprecated Gradle 9&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;mainClass&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;3&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;build.gradle&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;`sourceCompatibility`top-level forbidden Gradle 9&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Block`java { sourceCompatibility = JavaVersion.VERSION_21 }`&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;4&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;build.gradle&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Invalid Groovy assertion syntax&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;assert &amp;#8230;&amp;#8203; in [&quot;17&quot;, &quot;21&quot;, &quot;23&quot;, &quot;24&quot;]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;5&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;build.gradle&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Implicit dependency`compileKotlin` → &lt;code&gt;openApiGenerate&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;afterEvaluate { tasks.named(&quot;compileKotlin&quot;).dependsOn(&quot;openApiGenerate&quot;) }&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;6&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;gradle.properties&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;`gitPropertiesPluginVersion`incompatible Java 21&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;2.5.7&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;7&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Cache Gradle&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;docker-java 3.5.1 tested, resolved but insufficient&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Purge + passage docker-java 3.7.1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;8&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;build.gradle&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Testcontainers 1.20.6 incompatible with Docker Engine 29&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Forcing Testcontainers 2.0.5 + prefix`testcontainers-*`+ resolutionStrategy vs Spring Boot BOM&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_conclusion&quot;&gt;Conclusion&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If your JHipster/Gradle build crashes after an upgrade to Gradle 9 + Docker Engine 29, the errors fall into two categories:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build script errors&lt;/strong&gt;(the first 6): Gradle 9 removes properties and syntaxes that had been working for years.&lt;code&gt;sourceCompatibility=&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;main =&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;reportsDir&lt;/code&gt;). They are mechanical migrations once you know the new API.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Docker runtime errors&lt;/strong&gt;(the last two): Docker Engine 29.4.1 discards API clients &amp;lt; 1.40. Testcontainers 1.20.6 (imposed by Spring Boot 3.4.5) uses docker-java 3.4.1 which sends 1.32. Only Testcontainers 2.0.5 + docker-java 3.7.1 solves the problem, with the renaming of artifacts and forcing version via`resolutionStrategy.eachDependency`as the only way to bypass Spring Boot&amp;#8217;s implicit BOM.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Gradle build script at the root of the project is now clean.`./gradlew build`switches to Java 21, Gradle 9.4.1, Spring Boot 3.4.5 and Docker Engine 29.4.1.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_summary&quot;&gt;Summary&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When working with an AI agent like Opencode on complex projects across multiple sessions, you face a fundamental problem:&lt;strong&gt;the context leak&lt;/strong&gt;. The agent does not remember the previous session. Everything that was explained to them&amp;#8201;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8201;the architecture, the conventions, the state of the backlog&amp;#8201;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8201;is lost. Reconstructing this context each session is costly, slow, and a source of error.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This article sets out the artisanal strategy I built to solve this problem: a persistent governance system based on AsciiDoc files, with a dichotomy&lt;strong&gt;Eager/Lazy&lt;/strong&gt;to optimize context token consumption, and a&lt;strong&gt;essential end-of-session procedure&lt;/strong&gt;to ensure continuity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_scene_monday_21_april_900&quot;&gt;The Scene: Monday 21 April, 9:00&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I reopen Opencode to resume my Gradle plugin.&lt;code&gt;plantuml-plugin&lt;/code&gt;. Last night, I spent three hours discussing with the API key pool architecture agent&amp;#8201;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8201;round-robin rotation, quota management, automatic fallback. This morning, the agent looks at me with goldfish eyes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em&gt;_ Hello, I am your Opencode assistant. How can I help you today? &lt;/em&gt;_&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No&amp;#8201;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8201;Ah yes, the API key pool, we were at the YAML structure. No&amp;#8201;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8201;Attention,&lt;code&gt;PlantumlManager`is a Kotlin singleton object, not a class. No&amp;#8201;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8201;No, we decided yesterday that`SyntaxValidationResult`there remained a nested sealed class in`PlantumlService&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Everything has to be redone. Or rather: everything has to be re‑explained. I will spend the first twenty minutes of my session reconstructing a context that the agent already had in hand yesterday. Twenty minutes of burned tokens. Twenty minutes where I could be coding, but I am doing mandatory pedagogical work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It&amp;#8217;s not a bug in Opencode. It&amp;#8217;s the very nature of conversational LLMs: between two sessions, the working memory is&lt;strong&gt;completely erased&lt;/strong&gt;. The agent does not remember the previous mission, the decisions taken, the identified pitfalls, the code we wrote together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I&amp;#8217;ve experienced that dozens of times. On four simultaneous projects. With sessions that chain over weeks. I calculated: on average,&lt;strong&gt;30-40% of session time&lt;/strong&gt;was dedicated to recontextualizing the agent. At session 87 of the project`plantuml-plugin`, I cracked. I could no longer afford to explain for the tenth time that`AttemptEntry`is a top-level data class in`DiagramProcessor.kt`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I needed a system. Not a hack. Real governance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_genesis_from_chaos_to_method&quot;&gt;Genesis: From Chaos to Method&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_early_sessions_the_age_of_darkness&quot;&gt;The Early Sessions: The Age of Darkness&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My first project with Opencode,&lt;code&gt;plantuml-plugin&lt;/code&gt;, started without any governance. I ask a question, the agent answers, we iterate, the session ends, and the next day we start from zero. It was session 1, then 2, then 3&amp;#8230;&amp;#8203; up to session 62 where I realized I had lost cumulative hours re-explaining the same architecture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At session 62, the numbers are there:&lt;strong&gt;198 unit tests pass&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;42 functional tests validated&lt;/strong&gt;, the plugin works. But the cognitive cost is unbearable. Each new session begins with a twenty-minute monologue on the project structure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_destroyed_episode_of_site_yml_session_2_bakery_plugin&quot;&gt;The Destroyed Episode of site.yml (Session 2, bakery-plugin)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The method also arises from a catastrophe. On the project`bakery-gradle`, at session 2, I ask the agent to modify the file`site.yml`. The agent, without checking whether the file is versioned, makes a`Write`complete that overwrites the content. Result: the real tokens (Firebase API keys, deployment secrets) are replaced with fake placeholders. The file wasn&amp;#8217;t in git&amp;#8201;&amp;#8212;&amp;#8201;it was in`.gitignore`to protect the secrets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Without backup. Without`git restore`possible. I am stuck. I need to manually rebuild the configuration file, retrieve the tokens from my password managers, and put everything back together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is from this frustration that the&lt;strong&gt;Absolute Rule 1b&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em&gt;_ &lt;strong&gt;Never crush&lt;/strong&gt;a config file with a`Write`complete when a`Edit`Partial suffices.&lt;strong&gt;Never replace&lt;/strong&gt;sensitive values with dummy values.&lt;strong&gt;Check &lt;code&gt;git check-ignore&lt;/code&gt; and `git ls-files&lt;/strong&gt;before any modification. &lt;/em&gt;_&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This rule, now etched in stone in all my files`AGENT.adoc` et `INDEX.adoc`on four projects, was born from a real error that cost me an hour of manual work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_markdown_asciidoc_migration_session_1_cheroliv_com&quot;&gt;The Markdown → AsciiDoc Migration (Session 1, cheroliv.com)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On April 25, 2026, on`cheroliv.com`, I am making a radical decision: converting the entirety of Markdown governance to AsciiDoc. It&amp;#8217;s not aesthetic. It&amp;#8217;s functional. AsciiDoc offers a semantic structure that LLMs read better: hierarchical sections, typed tables, admonitions (&lt;code&gt;NOTE&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;WARNING&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;CAUTION&lt;/code&gt;), machine-readable document attributes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The session 1 of`cheroliv.com`formalize the structure :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Conversion of`AGENTS.md` en &lt;code&gt;AGENT.adoc&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Creating the specialized agents:`CODER.adoc`, &lt;code&gt;SCRUM_MASTER.adoc&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;PLANTUML_DESIGNER.adoc&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Creation of the Eager/Lazy structure:`INDEX.adoc`, &lt;code&gt;SESSIONS_HISTORY.adoc&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;AGENT_SESSION_MANAGER.adoc&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;SESSION_CHECKLIST.adoc&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;PROCEDURES.adoc&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Only one commit:`90975e9 refactor: migrate agent governance from Markdown to AsciiDoc`. And the site continues to operate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;diag-timeline&quot; class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
