&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Eager (Dashboard)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Lazy (Owner&amp;#8217;s Manual)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Size&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&amp;lt; 100 lines, &amp;lt; 10k tokens&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Unlimited, detailed&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Loading&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Auto, at the beginning of the session&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;At the request of the agent&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Content&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Absolute rules, current mission, critical state&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Session archives, complete history, detailed procedures, technical references&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Orient the agent immediately&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Answer deep context questions&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_eager_files_the_dashboard&quot;&gt;Eager Files: The Dashboard&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These files live at the root of each project and are automatically loaded by the agent at the start of each session. They form the&lt;strong&gt;dashboard&lt;/strong&gt;-- critical information, immediately accessible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;diag-eager-lazy&quot; class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 6) ]

@startuml
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam wrapWidth 200

package &quot;Project Root (Eager - Auto-loaded)&quot; {
    component &quot;&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;AGENT.adoc&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;
^^^^^
 Syntax Error? (Assumed diagram type: class)

@startuml
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam wrapWidth 200

package &quot;Project Root (Eager - Auto-loaded)&quot; {
    component &quot;&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;AGENT.adoc&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;
Absolute rules
Structure &amp;amp; Conventions&quot; as AGENT
    component &quot;&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;PROMPT_REPRISE.adoc&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;
Mission of the session N
Summary N-1&quot; as PROMPT
    component &quot;&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;INDEX.adoc&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;\nEntry point\nRules + Sessions&quot; as INDEX
    component &quot;&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;*_ESSENTIALS.adoc&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;
Business context
critical&quot; as ESS
}

package &quot;.agents/ (Lazy - Loaded on demand)&quot; {
    component &quot;&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;sessions/N-*.adoc&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;
Detailed archives
Decisions &amp;amp; Output&quot; as SESS
    component &quot;&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;SESSIONS_HISTORY.adoc&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;\nSummary table\nDate/Type/Score&quot; as HIST
    component &quot;&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;PROCEDURES.adoc&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;\nEnd-of-session templates\n6 steps\n&quot; as PROC
    component &quot;&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;*_REFERENCE.adoc&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;
Complete architecture
Technical references&quot; as REF
    component &quot;&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;COMPLETED_TASKS_ARCHIVE&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;\nCompleted tasks\nPer month&quot; as ARCH
    component &quot;&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;AGENT_MODUS_OPERANDI.adoc&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;\nDocumentation strategy\nMethodology&quot; as MOD
    component &quot;&amp;lt;b&amp;gt;*_REFERENCE.adoc&amp;lt;/b&amp;gt;\nBoot tests, A/B partition\nSpecific contexts&quot; as SPEC
}

AGENT --&amp;gt; PROMPT : &quot;References&quot;
AGENT --&amp;gt; INDEX : &quot;References&quot;
INDEX --&amp;gt; SESS : &quot;Index&quot;
INDEX --&amp;gt; HIST : &quot;Index&quot;
INDEX --&amp;gt; PROC : &quot;Reference&quot;
INDEX --&amp;gt; ARCH : &quot;Reference&quot;
INDEX --&amp;gt; REF : &quot;Reference&quot;
PROMPT --&amp;gt; SESS : &quot;Archive N-1&quot;
PROMPT --&amp;gt; ESS : &quot;Business context N&quot;

@enduml&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AGENT.adoc&lt;/strong&gt;-- The master file. On`cheroliv.com`, it is 200 lines long and contains :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The absolute rules of the project (no commit without permission, no`rm`without confirmation)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The project structure and code conventions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The essential commands (&lt;code&gt;./gradlew serve&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;./gradlew test&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The epics and the product backlog (prioritized user stories)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The cross-cutting quality criteria (accessibility, responsive, compatibility)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On`bakery-plugin`, Rule 0 is different :&lt;strong&gt;./gradlew -q publishToMavenLocal` mandatory after each source code change&lt;/strong&gt;. Because testing the plugin without republishing the local JAR cost me an hour debugging code that wasn&amp;#8217;t yet packaged.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PROMPT_REPRISE.adoc&lt;/strong&gt;-- The mission of the current session. Updated at the end of each session, it contains:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The session number and the priority mission&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The summary of the previous session (what has been done, what remains to be done)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The acceptance criteria of the current session&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The specific technical reminders&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;.agents/INDEX.adoc&lt;/strong&gt;The entry point. It summarizes the absolute rules, recent sessions, and especially the&lt;strong&gt;project portfolio&lt;/strong&gt;managed using the same methodology. To date, five projects are listed there:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;----
----
| magic-stick    | Session 23 | SCRIPT_VERIFICATION.adoc | 2026-04-27 |
| bakery-gradle  | Session 11 | TEST_COVERAGE_ANALYSIS   | 2026-04-27 |
| cheroliv.com   | Session 9  | TEST_COVERAGE_ANALYSIS   | 2026-04-27 |
| plantuml-gradle| Session 133| TEST_COVERAGE_ANALYSIS   | 2026-04-23 |
| jhipster-gradle-plugins | Session 1 | TEST_COVERAGE_ANALYSIS | 2026-04-28 |
----

**`*_ESSENTIALS.adoc`** -- A recent addition (Session 109, plantuml-plugin) to further optimize the Eager context. Instead of loading 200 lines of business context on the API key pool, I load 50 lines of the essential, and the remaining 150 lines stay LAZY in`*_REFERENCE.adoc`.

Measured result: passage of**~25k tokens EAGER to ~10k tokens**(60% gain). The agent no longer needs energy-consuming reminders.

==== The Missing Link: `opencode.json

I must confess something I almost forgot to document. Above all these .adoc files, there is a tiny JSON file without which nothing works. It&#39;s called`opencode.json`and it is six lines. Literally six lines.

[source,json]
----
{
  &quot;$schema&quot;: &quot;https://opencode.ai/config.json&quot;,
  &quot;instructions&quot;: [
    &quot;AGENT.adoc&quot;
  ]
}
----

This file tells Opencode: &quot;At startup, load`AGENT.adoc`Automatically. Without him, the agent is a blank page exactly as I described at the beginning of the article. With him, the agent already has in hand the absolute rules, the project architecture, and the essential commands — even before I say hello.

I discovered the importance of this file by chance. On`bakery-plugin`, it did not exist. I was wondering why the agent was systematically more &#39;lost&#39; on this project than on the others. The absolute rules were well in`AGENT.adoc`— but`AGENT.adoc`It was never loaded. The agent only read what I told him to read, manually, each session. This was session 11 of`bakery-plugin`when I realized the absence of the`opencode.json`. I created it — and session 12 started like the others.

This file is so obvious to me now that I wasn&#39;t even thinking about it anymore. A classic mistake of a developer who knows their tool too well. Nowadays, I systematically create it *before`AGENT.adoc`. This is the first stone.

==== The Duality of `INDEX.adoc

Another subtlety that deserves to be clarified:`INDEX.adoc`lives in`.agents/`— a folder that I presented as LAZY. However, I list it as EAGER in all my tables. There is an apparent tension here.

The field reality: the files`.agents/INDEX.adoc`are automatically loaded correctly at the beginning of the session, just as`AGENT.adoc` et `PROMPT_REPRISE.adoc`. They are in`.agents/`for organizational reasons — not to invade the root — but their behavior is EAGER.

on`plantuml-plugin`, `INDEX.adoc`is 200 lines long and contains the absolute *complete* rules with their history (the lessons from past sessions), the EPICs with scores, and the project portfolio. It is the document the agent consults to know &#39;where we stand&#39;. Sur`bakery-plugin`, it makes 150 lines with the roadmap and recent sessions.

The deliberate redundancy between`AGENT.adoc` et `INDEX.adoc`can be surprising. The absolute rules are present in both. Why? Because they fulfill two different roles: in`AGENT.adoc`, they are *explanatory* (the storytelling of the rule, the lesson learned) ; in`INDEX.adoc`, they are *executive* (the naked rule, without justification, for a quick consultation). The agent reads`AGENT.adoc`once to *understand*; he rereads`INDEX.adoc`for each session to *apply*. Two uses, two formats.

[plantuml, format=svg, id=diag-dualite-agent-index, alt=&quot;Comparaison entre AGENT.adoc (narratif) et INDEX.adoc (exécutif)&quot;]
----
@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

title Duality AGENT.adoc ←→ INDEX.adoc
left to right direction

rectangle &quot;AGENT.adoc
(Root — EAGER)&quot; as AGENT #E3F2FD {
  rectangle &quot;📖 **Narrative Format**
The storytelling of the rule
the lesson learned, the contexte

Wait, &quot;le contexte&quot; translates to &quot;the context&quot;. So correct:

📖 **Narrative Format**
The storytelling of the rule
the lesson learned, the context

Check: original third line: &quot;la leçon apprise, le contexte&quot;. Yes translation: &quot;the lesson learned, the context&quot;. Output that.

&amp;lt;/think&amp;gt;

�📖 **Narrative Format**
The storytelling of the rule
the lesson learned, the context&quot; as NARR
  rectangle &quot;🏗️ **Complete Architecture**
Project structure, components
Detailed US backlog&quot; as ARCHI
  rectangle &quot;�📋 **Explanatory Rules**
Why the rule exists
Incident history&quot; as EXPL
}

rectangle &quot;INDEX.adoc\n(.agents/ — EAGER)&quot; as INDEX #E8F5E9 {
  rectangle &quot;�⚡ **Executive Format**
The naked rule, without justification
Quick consultation&quot; as EXEC
  rectangle &quot;📊 **Roadmap &amp;amp; EPICs**\nSummary table\nProgress, Score, Priority&quot; as ROAD
  rectangle &quot;�🌐 **Projects Portfolio**
Cross‑sectional view
5 synchronized projects&quot; as PORT
}

AGENT --&amp;gt; INDEX : &quot;Agent reads AGENT.adoc\nonce to understand&quot;
INDEX --&amp;gt; AGENT : &quot;Agent re-reads INDEX.adoc\n each session to **apply**&quot;

note bottom of AGENT
  Taille max : 200 lignes
end note

