end note&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;legend bottom&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;= Couleur&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;= Projet&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&amp;lt;#E1BEE7&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;magic-stick — ISO Linux live&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&amp;lt;#FFE0B2&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;bakery-gradle — Plugin JBake&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&amp;lt;#C8E6C9&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;cheroliv.com — Site personnel&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&amp;lt;#BBDEFB&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;plantuml-gradle — Plugin IA&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&amp;lt;#FFCDD2&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div id=&quot;toc&quot; class=&quot;toc&quot;&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;toctitle&quot;&gt;Table des matières&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;sectlevel1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_the_scene_four_screenshots_two_renders&quot;&gt;The scene: four screenshots, two renders&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;sectlevel2&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_rendered_locally&quot;&gt;Rendered locally&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_online_rendering&quot;&gt;Online rendering&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_the_diagnosis_serve_was_not_pointing_to_the_correct_folder&quot;&gt;The diagnosis: &lt;code&gt;serve&lt;/code&gt; was not pointing to the correct folder&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_root_cause_jbake_cli_does_not_work_like_that&quot;&gt;Root cause: JBake CLI does not work like that&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_the_solution_positional_arguments_not_flags&quot;&gt;The solution: positional arguments, not flags&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_quick_check_with_curl&quot;&gt;Quick check with curl&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_why_this_bug_was_vicious&quot;&gt;Why this bug was vicious&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_conclusion&quot;&gt;Conclusion&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;preamble&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;reading time : 10 minutes&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You know that moment when your local site looks like nothing, but once deployed online everything is perfect? That&amp;#8217;s what happened to me with my Gradle JBake plugin. The task`serve`displayed square buttons, dark text on a black background, and a CSS strangely missing. However`publishSite`It was generating the same site, which itself was flawless. The culprit was neither the CSS, nor the browser, nor the cache. It was a line of Kotlin code — and a bad habit with command‑line arguments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;dlist&quot;&gt;
&lt;dl&gt;
&lt;dt class=&quot;hdlist1&quot;&gt;tic&lt;/dt&gt;
&lt;dd&gt;
&lt;p&gt;[]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/dd&gt;
&lt;/dl&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_scene_four_screenshots_two_renders&quot;&gt;The scene: four screenshots, two renders&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It was after a system crash. I had taken four screenshots to compare the local rendering (&lt;code&gt;./gradlew serve`on`localhost:8820&lt;/code&gt;) with the inline rendering (`publishSite`on GitHub Pages). Two screenshots per page: the top and the bottom.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_rendered_locally&quot;&gt;Rendered locally&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Top of page&lt;/strong&gt;— The buttons &lt;strong&gt;Project&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Template&lt;/strong&gt; are&lt;strong&gt;small, rectangular&lt;/strong&gt;, standard colors (blue and green). The card &lt;strong&gt;Start Writing&lt;/strong&gt; has a&lt;strong&gt;plain black background&lt;/strong&gt;, without frame.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/screen_local1.png&quot; alt=&quot;Rendu local - haut de page&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Footer&lt;/strong&gt;— The subtitle &lt;strong&gt;&quot;Derniers articles et ressources&quot;&lt;/strong&gt; is&lt;strong&gt;almost illegible&lt;/strong&gt;, too dark on black background. The dates under the blog images (&quot;17 October 2013&quot;, etc.) are&lt;strong&gt;absent&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/screen_local2.png&quot; alt=&quot;Rendu local - bas de page&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_online_rendering&quot;&gt;Online rendering&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Top of page&lt;/strong&gt;— The same buttons are&lt;strong&gt;large, ovaux, flashy neon green&lt;/strong&gt;, text in uppercase. The card has a&lt;strong&gt;rounded white frame with drop shadow&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/screen_online1.png&quot; alt=&quot;Rendu en ligne - haut de page&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bottom of page&lt;/strong&gt;— The subtitle is&lt;strong&gt;well readable&lt;/strong&gt;. The dates are&lt;strong&gt;visible&lt;/strong&gt;. The item cards have&lt;strong&gt;rounded corners&lt;/strong&gt;and the titles are&lt;strong&gt;in bold&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/screen_online2.png&quot; alt=&quot;Rendu en ligne - bas de page&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;First reflex: the theme. I use a dynamic theme system (light, dark, high-contrast) based on`localStorage`. Maybe the local store triggered a high-contrast theme? No. I had already writtenhttps://cheroliv.com/blog/2025/0098_preloading_css_variable_post.html[an entire article on the preloading of themes], I know how it works. And then, even in high-contrast mode, the CSS structure (oval buttons, shadows) should have been there. It wasn&amp;#8217;t there.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Second reflex: the browser cache. No, I had run the test with clean profiles. The diff persisted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Third reflex:`serve`was not serving the same files as`publishSite`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_diagnosis_serve_was_not_pointing_to_the_correct_folder&quot;&gt;The diagnosis: &lt;code&gt;serve&lt;/code&gt; was not pointing to the correct folder&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;My Gradle plugin`bakery`has two main tasks:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;bake&lt;/code&gt;: generates the static site in`build/bake/`&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;serve&lt;/code&gt;: launches a local web server&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;publishSite&lt;/code&gt;: push`build/bake/`to GitHub Pages&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The divergence could only come from`serve`. Si &lt;code&gt;publishSite`was publishing the correct content, it&amp;#8217;s that`build/bake/`was good. If`serve`what it was showing, however, was that it wasn&amp;#8217;t useful`build/bake/&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;#8217;s look at the code. In`SiteManager.kt`, the task`serve`is defined as follows:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;SiteManager.kt — La tâche serve (version buggy)&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;tasks.register(&quot;serve&quot;, JavaExec::class.java) { task -&amp;gt;
    task.apply {
        mainClass.set(&quot;org.jbake.launcher.Main&quot;)
        classpath = jbakeRuntime
        environment(&quot;GEM_PATH&quot;, jbakeRuntime.asPath)
        jvmArgs(/* ... */)
        args = listOf(
            &quot;-b&quot;, file(site.bake.srcPath).absolutePath,
            &quot;-s&quot;, layout.buildDirectory.get()
                .asFile.resolve(site.bake.destDirPath)
                .absolutePath
        )
    }
}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;org.jbake.launcher.Main`is the entry point of the JBake 2.7.0 CLI. The idea: to pass&lt;/code&gt;-b`for the source folder and`-s`for the destination folder, then start the server mode. But&amp;#8230;&amp;#8203;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_root_cause_jbake_cli_does_not_work_like_that&quot;&gt;Root cause: JBake CLI does not work like that&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JBake 2.7.0 is waiting for&lt;strong&gt;positional arguments&lt;/strong&gt;for source and destination, then optional flags. The signature is:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-text hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;text&quot;&gt;jbake &amp;lt;source&amp;gt; &amp;lt;destination&amp;gt; [options]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;However, in my code, I was writing :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-text hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;text&quot;&gt;args = listOf(&quot;-b&quot;, &quot;/path/to/site&quot;, &quot;-s&quot;, &quot;/path/to/build/bake&quot;)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JBake interpreted it as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;-b&lt;/code&gt;→ parse the &quot;bake&quot; flag (boolean), consumed&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;/path/to/site&lt;/code&gt;→ becomes positional argument 1 (source)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;-s&lt;/code&gt;→ parse the &quot;serve&quot; flag (boolean), server started&lt;strong&gt;immediately&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;/path/to/build/bake&lt;/code&gt;→ becomes an orphan argument, ignored or misinterpreted&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Result: Result: JBake was taking&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;lt;/think&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Result: JBake was taking`/path/to/site`as a source,&lt;strong&gt;did not take into account the destination&lt;/strong&gt;provided (&lt;code&gt;build/bake&lt;/code&gt;), and used its default directory (often`./output`or a temporary copy). The file`css/styles.css`the build was therefore overwritten or ignored, and it was an old default CSS (without custom variables, without rounded corners, without shadows) that was served.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In comparison,&lt;code&gt;bake&lt;/code&gt; et &lt;code&gt;publishSite`use the&lt;strong&gt;Official Gradle JBake plugin&lt;/strong&gt;( &amp;lt;/think&amp;gt; (`jbake-gradle-plugin&lt;/code&gt;) who writes neatly in`build/bake/`via the Gradle API. They do not pass through the CLI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_solution_positional_arguments_not_flags&quot;&gt;The solution: positional arguments, not flags&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The fix is trivial — once you know. All you have to do is pass source and destination as positional arguments, then`-s`finally :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;SiteManager.kt — La tâche serve (version corrigée)&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-kotlin hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;kotlin&quot;&gt;args = listOf(
    file(site.bake.srcPath).absolutePath,
    layout.buildDirectory.get()
        .asFile.resolve(site.bake.destDirPath)
        .absolutePath,
    &quot;-s&quot;
)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That&amp;#8217;s it. Three lines changed, bug fixed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;After local publication of the plugin (&lt;code&gt;publishToMavenLocal&lt;/code&gt;), un `./gradlew serve`Launch JBake with the correct syntax :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-text hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;text&quot;&gt;jbake /home/user/project/site /home/user/project/build/bake -s&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And this time, the Jetty server embedded in JBake serves the content of`build/bake/`— identical to what is published online.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/serve-vs-publish-diagram.svg&quot; alt=&quot;serve vs publish diagram&quot; width=&quot;1141&quot; height=&quot;348&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_quick_check_with_curl&quot;&gt;Quick check with curl&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To make sure the server serves the right content, a simple`curl`confirms that`index.html`contains`data-bs-theme=&quot;light&quot;`and that`build/bake/css/styles.css`weighs exactly 31,402 bytes — identical to the file generated by`bake`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ ./gradlew serve
# Dans un autre terminal :
$ curl -s http://localhost:8820/ | grep data-bs-theme
&amp;lt;html ... data-bs-theme=&quot;light&quot; ...&amp;gt;

$ curl -I http://localhost:8820/css/styles.css
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Length: 31402
Content-Type: text/css&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The local rendering is now&lt;strong&gt;pixel-identical&lt;/strong&gt;to the deployed rendering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_why_this_bug_was_vicious&quot;&gt;Why this bug was vicious&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You see why it was hard to catch?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No explicit error&lt;/strong&gt;JBake wasn&amp;#8217;t crashing. It &#39;worked&#39;, simply with a bad folder.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The build was working&lt;/strong&gt;:`./gradlew bake`was correctly generating the files in`build/bake/`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The deployment was working&lt;/strong&gt;:`publishSite`was pushing the right content online&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Only &lt;code&gt;serve&lt;/code&gt; was broken&lt;/strong&gt;: the development task, the one we constantly use to iterate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The habit of &lt;code&gt;-key value&lt;/strong&gt;As a developer, we are conditioned by years of Unix CLI&lt;/code&gt;-o output`, &lt;code&gt;-i input&lt;/code&gt;). JBake CLI is an exception — source and destination are positional.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_conclusion&quot;&gt;Conclusion&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you maintain a Gradle plugin that wraps JBake (or any CLI tool),&lt;strong&gt;read the arguments&#39; doc&lt;/strong&gt;even if you think you know them. An implicit assumption (&lt;code&gt;-s&lt;/code&gt;= &quot;set destination&quot;) can cost you hours of visual debugging.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here, the fix was literally to change:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-text hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;text&quot;&gt;args = listOf(&quot;-b&quot;, src, &quot;-s&quot;, dest)   // ❌ BUG&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;en :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-text hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;text&quot;&gt;args = listOf(src, dest, &quot;-s&quot;)         // ✅ FIX&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Three tokens moved, and my local site is once again as beautiful as the production site.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lesson&lt;/strong&gt;: when the rendering differs between local and prod without obvious reason, first suspect the &lt;strong&gt;pipeline&lt;/strong&gt; — not the CSS, not the browser, and even less the framework. It&amp;#8217;s often the step just before rendering that cheats.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div id=&quot;toc&quot; class=&quot;toc&quot;&gt;
&lt;div id=&quot;toctitle&quot;&gt;Table des matières&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;sectlevel1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_the_scene_a_blind_agent_in_a_world_of_tools&quot;&gt;The scene: a blind agent in a world of tools&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_anatomy_of_the_bug_two_shells_two_worlds&quot;&gt;Anatomy of the bug: two shells, two worlds&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_the_culprits_zshrc_vs_zshenv&quot;&gt;The culprits: .zshrc vs .zshenv&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_step_by_step_diagnostic&quot;&gt;Step-by-step diagnostic&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;sectlevel2&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_1_check_the_agents_path&quot;&gt;1. Check the agent&amp;#8217;s PATH&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_2_identify_what_is_in_zshrc_but_not_in_zshenv&quot;&gt;2. Identify what is in .zshrc but not in .zshenv&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_3_check_if_zshenv_exists&quot;&gt;3. Check if .zshenv exists&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_the_solution_zshenv_the_right_paths&quot;&gt;The solution: .zshenv + the right paths&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;sectlevel2&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_create_zshenv_with_all_the_essential_paths&quot;&gt;Create .zshenv with all the essential paths&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_why_not_source_sdkman_init_sh_in_zshenv&quot;&gt;Why not &lt;code&gt;source sdkman-init.sh&lt;/code&gt; in .zshenv?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_the_nvm_case_when_the_version_manager_forgets_to_leave_a_trace&quot;&gt;The NVM case: when the version manager forgets to leave a trace&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;sectlevel2&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_the_nvm_problem&quot;&gt;The NVM problem&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_the_solution_create_the_symlink_current_for_nvm&quot;&gt;The solution: create the symlink &lt;code&gt;current&lt;/code&gt; for NVM&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_automate_the_symlink_update&quot;&gt;Automate the symlink update&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;#_summary_table_of_paths&quot;&gt;Summary table of paths&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
