&lt;div id=&quot;preamble&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;reading time : 10 minutes&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You throw`./gradlew build`, the terminal is blocked for 3 minutes, and you need to do something else &lt;em&gt;while waiting&lt;/em&gt;? No need to open a new tab.`Ctrl+Z`suspends the process,`fg`It brings it back exactly where you left it. It&amp;#8217;s the most underrated Unix tip in a developer&amp;#8217;s daily routine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;dlist&quot;&gt;
&lt;dl&gt;
&lt;dt class=&quot;hdlist1&quot;&gt;knock&lt;/dt&gt;
&lt;dd&gt;
&lt;p&gt;[]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/dd&gt;
&lt;/dl&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_problem_a_busy_terminal&quot;&gt;The problem: a busy terminal&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every developer has experienced this situation:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ ./gradlew build
&amp;gt; Building...&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The terminal is frozen. You can no longer type any command. And you need to consult a file, run a`git status`, or check a busy port.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 6) ]

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE

actor Développeur as dev
participant &quot;terminal&quot; as term
participant &quot;Gradle
^^^^^
 Syntax Error? (Assumed diagram type: sequence)

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE

actor Développeur as dev
participant &quot;terminal&quot; as term
participant &quot;Gradle
( process )&quot; as gradle

dev -&amp;gt; term : ./gradlew build
term -&amp;gt; gradle : Lance le build
gradle -&amp;gt; term : Occupe le terminal\n(pas de prompt)
dev -&amp;gt; term : veut taper une commande
term --&amp;gt; dev : ❌ Terminal bloqué

note right of dev
  Le développeur est
  paralysé pendant
  toute la durée du build
end note
@enduml&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most developers open a new terminal. But there is a more elegant, faster, and native solution: job management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_three_essential_commands&quot;&gt;The three essential commands&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_ctrlz_suspend_sigtstp&quot;&gt;Ctrl+Z — Suspend (SIGTSTP)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;`Ctrl+Z`sends the signal`SIGTSTP`to the foreground process. The process is&lt;strong&gt;suspended&lt;/strong&gt;— not killed — and the terminal regains its prompt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ ./gradlew build
&amp;gt; Building...
^Z
[1]+  Stoppé    ./gradlew build
$&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The number in brackets`[1]`is the&lt;strong&gt;job number&lt;/strong&gt;. Le `+`indicates the default job.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_fg_bring_to_foreground&quot;&gt;fg — Bring to foreground&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;`fg`brings the suspended job to the foreground. The process resumes exactly where it left off.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ fg
./gradlew build
&amp;gt; Building... (reprend où il en était)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With a specific job number:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ fg %2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_bg_resume_in_the_background&quot;&gt;bg — Resume in the background&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;`bg`Resume the process without blocking the terminal. Ideal for long builds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ bg
[1]+ ./gradlew build &amp;amp;
$&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Le `&amp;amp;`at the end means that the process is running in the background.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_jobs_list_the_shells_jobs&quot;&gt;jobs — List the shell&amp;#8217;s jobs&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ jobs
[1]-  Stoppé    vim README.md
[2]+  En cours   ./gradlew build&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 5) ]

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

state &quot;Foreground
^^^^^
 Syntax Error? (Assumed diagram type: sequence)

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

state &quot;Foreground
(blocked terminal)&quot; as fg #LightCoral
state &quot;Suspended\n(Ctrl+Z)&quot; as stopped #LightYellow
state &quot;Background
(bg)&quot; as bg_ #LightGreen

[*] --&amp;gt; fg : Lance une commande
fg --&amp;gt; stopped : Ctrl+Z\n(SIGTSTP)
stopped --&amp;gt; fg : fg\nreprend en avant-plan
stopped --&amp;gt; bg_ : bg\nreprend en arrière-plan
bg_ --&amp;gt; fg : fg\nramène en avant-plan
fg --&amp;gt; [*] : Commande terminée

note right of stopped
  Le processus est figé
  mais _pas_ tué
end note

note left of bg_
  Le terminal est libre
  le build continue
end note
@enduml&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_scenario_1_the_long_build&quot;&gt;Scenario 1: The long build&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is the most common use case. You start a Gradle build, the terminal is blocked, and you need to do something else.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 8) ]

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
autonumber

actor Développeur as dev
participant &quot;Terminal&quot; as term
participant &quot;Gradle&quot; as gradle
database &quot;State
^^^^^
 Syntax Error? (Assumed diagram type: sequence)

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
autonumber

actor Développeur as dev
participant &quot;Terminal&quot; as term
participant &quot;Gradle&quot; as gradle
database &quot;State
process&quot; as state

dev -&amp;gt; term : ./gradlew build
term -&amp;gt; gradle : Lance le build
gradle -&amp;gt; state : En cours (FG)
dev -&amp;gt; term : Ctrl+Z
term -&amp;gt; state : Suspendu (job [1])
term --&amp;gt; dev : Prompt libre $

dev -&amp;gt; term : git status
term --&amp;gt; dev : working tree clean

dev -&amp;gt; term : fg
term -&amp;gt; state : Reprend (FG)
gradle --&amp;gt; dev : Build réussi ✓

note right of state
  Le processus Gradle
  n&#39;a jamais été tué
  Il reprend exactement
  où il s&#39;était arrêté
end note
@enduml&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_step_by_step&quot;&gt;Step by step&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ ./gradlew build
&amp;gt; Building...
^Z
[1]+  Stoppé    ./gradlew build

$ git status
On branch main
nothing to commit, working tree clean

$ fg
./gradlew build
&amp;gt; Building...
BUILD SUCCESSFUL in 2m 34s&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_scenario_2_the_forgotten_editor&quot;&gt;Scenario 2: The Forgotten Editor&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are in`vim`, you need to consult another file &lt;em&gt;without&lt;/em&gt; leaving`vim`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;# Dans vim, en mode commande :
:shell
$ cat /path/to/other/file.txt
$ exit
# Retour dans vim&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But it&amp;#8217;s heavy. With`Ctrl+Z`, it is immediate :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;# Dans vim, n&#39;importe quel moment :
Ctrl+Z
[1]+  Stoppé    vim README.md

$ cat /path/to/other/file.txt
# ... lire le fichier ...

$ fg
vim README.md
# Retour exact là où on en était, curseur en place&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/vim-suspend.svg&quot; alt=&quot;vim suspend&quot; width=&quot;410&quot; height=&quot;510&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock note&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-note&quot; title=&quot;Note&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;code&gt;vim`parfaitement restores its state after a`fg&lt;/code&gt;: cursor position, buffer content, undo history — everything is preserved.
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_scenario_3_the_opencode_process_suspended&quot;&gt;Scenario 3: The opencode process suspended&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is the scenario that motivated this article. You use`opencode`(CLI tool for running an LLM on your code), and the process is suspended.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 7) ]

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor Développeur as dev
participant &quot;opencode
^^^^^
 Syntax Error? (Assumed diagram type: sequence)

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor Développeur as dev
participant &quot;opencode
(LLM agent)&quot; as agent
participant &quot;Shell&quot; as shell
participant &quot;git&quot; as git

dev -&amp;gt; agent : Session active
agent -&amp;gt; agent : Tour de parole\ndu LLM en cours

note over agent
  Ctrl+Z arrive
  en plein milieu
  d&#39;une analyse de code
end note

dev -&amp;gt; agent : Ctrl+Z
agent -&amp;gt; shell : Suspendu (job [1])
dev -&amp;gt; git : git diff
git --&amp;gt; dev : changements visibles
dev -&amp;gt; shell : fg
shell -&amp;gt; agent : Reprend (job [1])
agent --&amp;gt; dev : Reprend exactement\nl&#39;analyse en cours

note right of agent
  Aucune perte de contexte
  Le LLM reprend sa réponse
  exactement où il en était
end note
@enduml&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ opencode
# ... session en cours, LLM analyse le code ...
^Z
[1]+  Stoppé    opencode

$ git diff HEAD~1
# vérifier les changements récents

$ fg
opencode
# Le LLM reprend là où il s&#39;était arrêté&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The advantage is twofold:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No loss of context&lt;/strong&gt;: the LLM session, conversation history, open files — everything is preserved&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No restart&lt;/strong&gt;: no need to restart opencode, reload the context, re-explain the problem to the LLM&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_scenario_4_managing_several_jobs_simultaneously&quot;&gt;Scenario 4: Managing several jobs simultaneously&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;fg&lt;/code&gt; et `bg`They accept a job number to target a specific process when multiple are suspended.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ vim config.yml
^Z
[1]+  Stoppé    vim config.yml

$ ./gradlew test
^Z
[2]+  Stoppé    ./gradlew test

$ htop
^Z
[3]+  Stoppé    htop

$ jobs
[1]   Stoppé    vim config.yml
[2]-  Stoppé    ./gradlew test
[3]+  Stoppé    htop

$ fg %2
./gradlew test
# Le build reprend en avant-plan

$ bg %3
[3] htop &amp;amp;
# htop reprend en arrière-plan&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 12) ]

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE

rectangle &quot;Suspended jobs&quot; as jobs #LightYellow {
  card &quot;[1] vim config.yml&quot; as j1
  card &quot;[2] ./gradlew test&quot; as j2
  card &quot;[3] htop&quot; as j3
}

rectangle &quot;Actions&quot; as actions #LightGreen {
  card &quot;fg %2
→ foreground&quot; as a1
^^^^^
 Syntax Error? (Assumed diagram type: activity)

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE

rectangle &quot;Suspended jobs&quot; as jobs #LightYellow {
  card &quot;[1] vim config.yml&quot; as j1
  card &quot;[2] ./gradlew test&quot; as j2
  card &quot;[3] htop&quot; as j3
}

rectangle &quot;Actions&quot; as actions #LightGreen {
  card &quot;fg %2
→ foreground&quot; as a1
  card &quot;bg %3\n→ background&quot; as a2
  card &quot;fg %1\n→ avant-plan&quot; as a3
}

jobs --&amp;gt; actions : fg/bg + numéro de job
actions --&amp;gt; j2 : Reprend
actions --&amp;gt; j3 : En arrière-plan

note bottom of jobs
  Chaque job conserve
  son état exact
  entre les suspend/resume
end note
@enduml&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_summary_of_job_commands&quot;&gt;Summary of job commands&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 20%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 40%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 40%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;Order&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;Effect&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;Example&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;Ctrl+Z&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Suspend the process in the foreground&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Sending of`SIGTSTP`&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;fg&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Resume the default job in the foreground&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;fg&lt;/code&gt; ou &lt;code&gt;fg %1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;fg %n&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Resume job n in the foreground&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;fg %2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;bg&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Resume the default job in the background&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;bg&lt;/code&gt; ou &lt;code&gt;bg %1&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;bg %n&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Resume job n in the background&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;bg %2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;jobs&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;List the jobs of the current shell&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;jobs -l&lt;/code&gt;(with PID)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;kill %n&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Finish the job n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;kill %2&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_differences_between_fg_bg_ctrlz_ctrlc_and&quot;&gt;Differences between fg, bg, Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+C and &amp;amp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Many developers confuse these mechanisms. Here is a decisive clarification.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 7) ]

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

rectangle &quot;**Ctrl+Z**\nSIGTSTP&quot; as ctrlz #LightYellow {
  card &quot;Suspend the process
(it is still in memory)
^^^^^
 Syntax Error? (Assumed diagram type: activity)

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

rectangle &quot;**Ctrl+Z**\nSIGTSTP&quot; as ctrlz #LightYellow {
  card &quot;Suspend the process
(it is still in memory)
Usable with fg/bg&quot; as c1
}

rectangle &quot;**Ctrl+C**\nSIGINT&quot; as ctrlc #LightCoral {
  card &quot;Kill the process\n(no return possible)\nLoss of all state&quot; as c2
}

rectangle &quot;**&amp;amp; **\n(background)&quot; as ampersand #LightGreen {
  card &quot;Launch directly
in the background
Free terminal immediately&quot; as c3
}

rectangle &quot;**fg**\n(foreground)&quot; as fg_ #SkyBlue {
  card &quot;Bring a job
suspended to the foreground
Terminal busy&quot; as c4
}

rectangle &quot;**bg**
(background)&quot; as bg_ #Lavender {
  card &quot;Resume a job
suspended in background
Terminal free&quot; as c5
}

ctrlz -right-&amp;gt; fg_ : fg pour reprendre
ctrlz -right-&amp;gt; bg_ : bg pour continuer\nen arrière-plan
ctrlc -right-&amp;gt; c2 : Pas de retour\nprocessus tué

note bottom of ctrlz
  Le processus est **figé**
  mais **pas tué**
end note

note bottom of ampersand
  Alternative : lancer
  ./gradlew build &amp;amp;
  directement en arrière-plan
end note
@enduml&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 16.6666%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 33.3333%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 16.6666%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 33.3335%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;Shortcut/Command&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;Signal&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;Effect&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;Go back?&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;Ctrl+Z&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;SIGTSTP&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Suspend the process (frozen, in memory)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Yes:`fg` ou &lt;code&gt;bg&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;Ctrl+C&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;SIGINT&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Kill the process (terminated)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;No: process destroyed&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;Ctrl+\&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;SIGQUIT&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Kill the process + core dump&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;No: process destroyed&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;commande &amp;amp;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;—&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Launch directly in the background&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;`fg`to bring it to the foreground&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;admonitionblock tip&quot;&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;icon&quot;&gt;
&lt;i class=&quot;fa icon-tip&quot; title=&quot;Tip&quot;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;code&gt;Ctrl+Z`is&lt;strong&gt;non-destructive&lt;/strong&gt;. The process is frozen as is, in memory. You can immediately resume with`fg&lt;/code&gt;. It&amp;#8217;s a &lt;em&gt;pause&lt;/em&gt;, not a &lt;em&gt;stop&lt;/em&gt;.
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_complete_life_cycle_of_a_job&quot;&gt;The complete life cycle of a job&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 7) ]

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

title Full life cycle of a shell job
state &quot;Nonexistent&quot; as none
state &quot;Foreground
^^^^^
 Syntax Error? (Assumed diagram type: state)

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

title Full life cycle of a shell job
state &quot;Nonexistent&quot; as none
state &quot;Foreground
(occupies the terminal)&quot; as foreground #LightCoral
state &quot;Suspended\n(Ctrl+Z / SIGTSTP)&quot; as suspended #LightYellow
state &quot;Background\n(bg or &amp;amp;)&quot; as background #LightGreen
state &quot;Finished
(exit code 0)&quot; as done #LightGray

[*] --&amp;gt; none
none --&amp;gt; foreground : tape une commande
foreground --&amp;gt; suspended : Ctrl+Z
foreground --&amp;gt; done : fin normale

suspended --&amp;gt; foreground : fg
suspended --&amp;gt; background : bg
suspended --&amp;gt; done : kill %n

background --&amp;gt; foreground : fg
background --&amp;gt; done : fin normale\n(en arrière-plan)
background --&amp;gt; suspended : Ctrl+Z\n(si fg puis Ctrl+Z)

done --&amp;gt; [*]

note right of suspended
  L&#39;état suspendu est
  le pivot de tout le
  système de jobs
end note
@enduml&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_advanced_tips&quot;&gt;Advanced tips&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_fg_with_the_most_recent_job_and_the_work_study&quot;&gt;fg with the most recent job and the work-study&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;fg`without argument brings back the marked job&lt;/code&gt;+&lt;code&gt;(the most recent). But you can also use&lt;/code&gt;%-`to target the previous job:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ vim file1.txt
^Z
[1]+  Stoppé    vim file1.txt

$ vim file2.txt
^Z
[2]+  Stoppé    vim file2.txt

$ fg      # ramène job [2] (le plus récent)
$ fg %-   # ramène job [1] (le précédent)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_to_kill_a_job_properly&quot;&gt;to kill a job properly&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ jobs
[1]-  Stoppé    vim config.yml
[2]+  Stoppé    ./gradlew test

$ kill %2       # envoie SIGTERM au job 2
$ kill -9 %1    # envoie SIGKILL au job 1 (force)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_disown_detach_from_the_shell&quot;&gt;disown : detach from the shell&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;disown`remove a job from the shell&amp;#8217;s jobs table. The process continues to run but can no longer be brought back with`fg&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ ./gradlew build &amp;amp;
[1] 12345

$ disown %1
# Le processus continue mais n&#39;est plus lié au shell
# Ça survives à la fermeture du terminal&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_combine_with_nohup_for_long_processes&quot;&gt;Combine with nohup for long processes&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In order for a process to survive terminal closure:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ nohup ./gradlew build &amp;amp;
[1] 12345
$ disown %1
# Le build continue même si vous fermez le terminal&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 7) ]

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

rectangle &quot;fg&quot; as fg_ #SkyBlue {
  card &quot;Bring back the most recent job
(+)&quot; as f1
^^^^^
 Syntax Error? (Assumed diagram type: activity)

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

rectangle &quot;fg&quot; as fg_ #SkyBlue {
  card &quot;Bring back the most recent job
(+)&quot; as f1
  card &quot;Target a specific job:
fg %n&quot; as f2
  card &quot;Alternates : fg %-&quot; as f3
}

rectangle &quot;kill %n&quot; as kill_ #LightCoral {
  card &quot;SIGTERM (clean)&quot; as k1
  card &quot;SIGKILL -9 (force)&quot; as k2
}

rectangle &quot;disown&quot; as disown #Lavender {
  card &quot;Detaches from the shell\n(survives disconnection)&quot; as d1
}

rectangle &quot;nohup + &amp;amp;&quot; as nohup_ #LightGreen {
  card &quot;Process immune
against SIGHUP
(survives terminal closure)&quot; as n1
}

fg_ -right-&amp;gt; kill_ : si faut\nterminer
kill_ -right-&amp;gt; disown_ : ou détacher
nohup_ -left-&amp;gt; fg_ : fg ramène en\navant-plan

note bottom of disown_
  Après disown, fg ne peut
  plus ramener le job
end note
@enduml&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_common_pitfalls_and_mistakes&quot;&gt;Common pitfalls and mistakes&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_confuse_ctrlz_and_ctrlc&quot;&gt;Confuse Ctrl+Z and Ctrl+C&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It&amp;#8217;s the most common error.`Ctrl+C`kill the process.`Ctrl+Z`it suspends. If you press on`Ctrl+C`Reflexively, the entire state is lost — open files, LLM sessions, builds in progress.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/ctrlz-vs-ctrlc.svg&quot; alt=&quot;ctrlz vs ctrlc&quot; width=&quot;1140&quot; height=&quot;129&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_jobs_are_local_to_the_shell&quot;&gt;Jobs are local to the shell&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;jobs&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;fg&lt;/code&gt; et `bg`only work in the shell that launched the processes. If you open a new terminal, you will not see the other&amp;#8217;s jobs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;# Terminal 1
$ vim file.txt
^Z
[1]+  Stoppé    vim file.txt

# Terminal 2 (nouveau)
$ jobs
# (rien — les jobs sont locaux au shell)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To view system-wide processes, use`ps` ou &lt;code&gt;htop&lt;/code&gt; :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;ps aux | grep vim&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_jobs_do_not_survive_shell_closure&quot;&gt;Jobs do not survive shell closure&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you close the terminal, all suspended or background jobs are destroyed. For a process to survive, use`nohup`&lt;br&gt;
+&lt;code&gt;disown&lt;/code&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;$ nohup ./gradlew build &amp;amp;
[1] 12345
$ disown %1
# Fermer le terminal → le build continue&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_interactive_processes_and_fg&quot;&gt;Interactive processes and fg&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Some interactive programs do not fare well after a`Ctrl+Z` + &lt;code&gt;fg&lt;/code&gt;. It&amp;#8217;s rare but it happens:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Some programs that use signals (vim, htop, less handle them well`Ctrl+Z`)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Long network programs (ssh, opencode) generally recover correctly&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Programs that modify the terminal (ncurses) can sometimes leave the terminal in an unexpected state.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In case of corrupted terminal after a`fg`, type:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;reset&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_summary_diagram&quot;&gt;Summary diagram&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 10) ]

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam ArrowColor #444444

title &quot;fg — The tip that changes everything&quot;

rectangle &quot;**Problem**&quot; as problem #LightCoral {
  card &quot;Terminal blocked
by a process&quot; as p1
^^^^^
 Syntax Error? (Assumed diagram type: activity)

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam ArrowColor #444444

title &quot;fg — The tip that changes everything&quot;

rectangle &quot;**Problem**&quot; as problem #LightCoral {
  card &quot;Terminal blocked
by a process&quot; as p1
  card &quot;Open a new\nterminal = heavy solution&quot; as p2
}

rectangle &quot;Solution&quot; as solution #LightGreen {
  card &quot;Ctrl+Z → suspend&quot; as s1
  card &quot;fg → resumes&quot; as s2
  card &quot;bg → in background&quot; as s3
  card &quot;jobs → view the suspended&quot; as s4
}

rectangle &quot;Advantages&quot; as advantages #SkyBlue {
  card &quot;No loss of context&quot; as a1
  card &quot;No restart&quot; as a2
  card &quot;One terminal is enough&quot; as a3
}

problem -right-&amp;gt; solution : &quot;The native
Unix solution for 40 years&quot;
solution -right-&amp;gt; advantages : &quot;Result&quot;

note bottom of advantages
  fg n&#39;est pas un tips obscur
  C&#39;est un mécanisme fondamental
  du shell Unix
end note
@enduml&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_why_fg_is_underestimated&quot;&gt;Why fg is underestimated&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most modern developers discover`fg`late, maybe never. Some reasons:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IDEs hide the terminal&lt;/strong&gt;: VS Code offers an integrated terminal, but multiple tabs make`fg`seemingly less necessary&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Graphical tools replace CLI&lt;/strong&gt;: file managers, system monitors, graphical Git clients&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;tmux and screen&lt;/strong&gt;: these multiplexers solve the same problem differently, but`fg`is simpler and always available&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;However,`fg`is :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Universal&lt;/strong&gt;: present in all POSIX shells (bash, zsh, fish&amp;#8230;&amp;#8203;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No dependence&lt;/strong&gt;: no need to install tmux or screen&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Snapshot&lt;/strong&gt;: two strikes (&lt;code&gt;Ctrl+Z`then`fg&lt;/code&gt;) to suspend and resume&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Context Preserver&lt;/strong&gt;: the process state is intact&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 8) ]

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

rectangle &quot;Why is fg underestimated?&quot; as why #LightCoral {
  card &quot;IDE with terminal\nmulti-tab&quot; as w1
  card &quot;Graphical tools
that replace the CLI&quot; as w2
^^^^^
 Syntax Error? (Assumed diagram type: activity)

@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif

rectangle &quot;Why is fg underestimated?&quot; as why #LightCoral {
  card &quot;IDE with terminal\nmulti-tab&quot; as w1
  card &quot;Graphical tools
that replace the CLI&quot; as w2
  card &quot;tmux/screen
solve the problem
otherwise&quot; as w3
}

rectangle &quot;Why fg is\nsuperior?&quot; as superior #LightGreen {
  card &quot;Universal : bash,\nzsh, fish, sh...&quot; as s1
  card &quot;No dependency:
no installation&quot; as s2
  card &quot;Two keystrokes:
Ctrl+Z then fg&quot; as s3
  card &quot;Context preserved :
zero loss of state&quot; as s4
}

why -right-&amp;gt; superior : &quot;Simplicity
always wins&quot;
@enduml&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_technical_memorandum_the_signals&quot;&gt;Technical memorandum: the signals&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For the curious, here are the signals involved:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;table class=&quot;tableblock frame-all grid-all stretch&quot;&gt;
&lt;colgroup&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 14.2857%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 28.5714%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 28.5714%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;col style=&quot;width: 28.5715%;&quot;&gt;
&lt;/colgroup&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;Signal&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;name&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;Sent by&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;Effect&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;2&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;SIGINT&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;Ctrl+C&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Interruption — terminates the process&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;3&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;SIGQUIT&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;Ctrl+\&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Exit with core dump&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;18&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;SIGTSTP&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;Ctrl+Z&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Interactive stop — suspend the process&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;19&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;SIGCONT&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;fg&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;bg&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Continue — resumes a suspended process&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;15&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;SIGTERM&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;kill %n&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Clean termination&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;9&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;SIGKILL&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;&lt;code&gt;kill -9 %n&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td class=&quot;tableblock halign-left valign-top&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;tableblock&quot;&gt;Forced termination (impossible to intercept)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The full stream :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;./images/signal-flow.svg&quot; alt=&quot;signal flow&quot; width=&quot;404&quot; height=&quot;525&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_conclusion&quot;&gt;Conclusion&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;`fg`It&amp;#8217;s not an obscure tip — it&amp;#8217;s a fundamental Unix shell mechanism, available since the 1970s. The fact that most developers ignore it is a symptom of our era: IDEs and multiplexers have distanced us from the basics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But when you are on an SSH server, in a minimal terminal, or simply when you&amp;#8217;re using`opencode`and the LLM is hard at work —&lt;code&gt;Ctrl+Z&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;fg&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;bg&lt;/code&gt;, `jobs`are your best friends.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em&gt;_ Ctrl+Z suspend, fg resume. It&amp;#8217;s the terminal&amp;#8217;s pause‑play. &lt;/em&gt;_&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
