&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_the_why_vs_code_in_the_home&quot;&gt;The Why: VS Code in the Home&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_problem_with_the_system_installation&quot;&gt;The problem with the system installation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;VS Code installed via`apt`, &lt;code&gt;dnf`or in&lt;/code&gt;/opt`lock the application files behind root privileges. Any modification of the native CSS, of`product.json`or the installation folder requires`sudo`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But, when one uses&lt;strong&gt;opencode&lt;/strong&gt;(CLI tool for driving an LLM on its code), the agent needs to be able to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Write in the configuration files`~/.config/Code/User/settings.json`) — that&amp;#8217;s already in the home&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Edit the IDE assets (workbench CSS,&lt;code&gt;product.json&lt;/code&gt;) for advanced customizations — that&amp;#8217;s blocked without sudo&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_the_solution_a_local_installation&quot;&gt;The solution: a local installation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We download the official tarball archive and extract it directly into`~/apps/`(nothing)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;mkdir -p ~/apps
cd ~/apps
wget &quot;https://code.visualstudio.com/sha/download?build=stable&amp;amp;os=linux-x64&quot; -O vscode.tar.gz
tar -xzf vscode.tar.gz
rm vscode.tar.gz&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The binary is then located in`~/apps/VSCode-linux-x64/bin/code`. None`sudo`is not necessary to read, edit, or replace any file under`~/apps/VSCode-linux-x64/`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_concrete_advantages&quot;&gt;Concrete advantages&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Failed to generate image: PlantUML preprocessing failed: [From &amp;lt;input&amp;gt; (line 12) ]

