&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_install_in_the_home_frees_everything&quot;&gt;Install in the home frees everything&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A local installation in`~/apps`gives full control over VS Code:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No`sudo`to modify the CSS or the configuration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The opencode+LLM agent can write to the config files and assets of the IDE.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Rollback trivial: Restore the timestamped backup&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_zoom_font_size_for_list_components&quot;&gt;zoom` &amp;gt; &lt;code&gt;font-size&lt;/code&gt; for list components&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;VS Code controls line height via JavaScript. Modify`font-size`without being able to touch the height allocated by the layout engine gives texts that overflow. The property`zoom`on the parent container scales everything proportionally and works around this problem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_custom_css_extension_requires_explicit_activation&quot;&gt;Custom CSS extension requires explicit activation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is not a &quot;set and forget&quot; setting. Every change to the custom CSS file requires re-running &quot;Enable Custom CSS and JS&quot; from the command palette (&lt;code&gt;Ctrl+Shift+P&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_an_update_script_is_indispensable&quot;&gt;An update script is indispensable&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Without a script, every VS Code update deletes the workbench CSS patches. The script`vscode-update.sh`automates the download, the replacement, the re-patch, and the cleaning of the checksums&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_quick_references&quot;&gt;Quick references&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;VS Code download: &lt;a href=&quot;https://code.visualstudio.com/Download&quot; class=&quot;bare&quot;&gt;https://code.visualstudio.com/Download&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Custom CSS and JSLoader Extension :`be5invis.vscode-custom-css`&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Issue VS Code requesting a native setting for the Explorer font:https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues/149[github.com/microsoft/vscode#149]&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

