&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_introduction&quot;&gt;Introduction&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In a world where digital privacy is increasingly threatened, &lt;strong&gt;Tor Browser&lt;/strong&gt; remains an essential tool for preserving one&amp;#8217;s anonymity and freedom of information. However, it is crucial never to run a downloaded software without having&lt;strong&gt;verified its authenticity&lt;/strong&gt;. This article presents a comprehensive method for :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Download &lt;strong&gt;Tor Browser&lt;/strong&gt; and its signature`.asc`&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check the validity of the downloaded file&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Install and launch &lt;strong&gt;Tor Browser&lt;/strong&gt; on Ubuntu&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Add it to the desktop menus for daily use&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Exploring educational and ethical OSINT resources via Tor&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_downloading_tor_and_its_signature&quot;&gt;Downloading Tor and its signature&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create a dedicated folder for the Tor browser:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;mkdir -p ~/workspace/tipiak/tor
cd ~/workspace/tipiak/tor&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Then download the Tor Browser archive and its signature:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;wget https://www.torproject.org/dist/torbrowser/14.5.7/tor-browser-linux-x86_64-14.5.7.tar.xz
wget https://www.torproject.org/dist/torbrowser/14.5.7/tor-browser-linux-x86_64-14.5.7.tar.xz.asc&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_cryptographic_verification_of_the_signature&quot;&gt;Cryptographic verification of the signature&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This step is&lt;strong&gt;indispensable&lt;/strong&gt;to ensure that the downloaded file indeed comes from the &lt;strong&gt;Tor Project&lt;/strong&gt; and has not been modified.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_1_import_the_tor_projects_public_key&quot;&gt;1. Import the Tor Project&amp;#8217;s public key&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;gpg --auto-key-locate nodefault,wkd --locate-keys torbrowser@torproject.org&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Check that the key is properly imported:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;gpg --list-keys torbrowser@torproject.org&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_2_verify_the_signature&quot;&gt;2. Verify the signature&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;gpg --verify tor-browser-linux-x86_64-14.5.7.tar.xz.asc tor-browser-linux-x86_64-14.5.7.tar.xz&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If everything is correct, the following message will be displayed:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;gpg: Good signature from &quot;Tor Browser Developers (signing key)&quot;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In case of an uncertified key warning, this simply means that you have not yet signed the Tor Project&amp;#8217;s trusted key, but the signature remains valid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_practical_case_valid_signature_but_uncertified_key&quot;&gt;Practical case: Valid signature but uncertified key&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is common to encounter a message like this one during verification:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-none hljs&quot;&gt;gpg --verify tor-browser-linux-x86_64-14.5.7.tar.xz.asc tor-browser-linux-x86_64-14.5.7.tar.xz
gpg: Signature faite le mar. 16 sept. 2025 14:26:26 CEST
gpg:                avec la clef RSA CAAE408AEBE2288E96FC5D5E157432CF78A65729
gpg: Bonne signature de « Tor Browser Developers (signing key) &amp;lt;torbrowser@torproject.org&amp;gt; » [inconnu]
gpg: Attention : cette clef n&#39;est pas certifiée avec une signature de confiance.
gpg:          Rien n&#39;indique que la signature appartient à son propriétaire.
Empreinte de clef principale : EF6E 286D DA85 EA2A 4BA7  DE68 4E2C 6E87 9329 8290
     Empreinte de la sous-clef : CAAE 408A EBE2 288E 96FC  5D5E 1574 32CF 78A6 5729&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This message indicates that the signature is technically &quot;good&quot; (the file has not been altered), but your GPG system cannot &lt;strong&gt;certify trust&lt;/strong&gt; in the key itself. To dispel this doubt, it is imperative to compare the fingerprint of the main key (&lt;code&gt;EF6E 286D DA85 EA2A 4BA7 DE68 4E2C 6E87 9329 8290&lt;/code&gt;) with that published on the official Tor Project website.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;According to the official site, the expected fingerprint is:`EF6E286DDA85EA2A4BA7DE684E2C6E8793298290`.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Since the displayed footprint by`gpg`matches &lt;strong&gt;exactly&lt;/strong&gt; that of the official site, you can be certain that the key is legitimate and the file is safe. The warning of &quot;untrusted key&quot; is then information about your local GPG configuration, and not about the validity of the signature or the authenticity of the file.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_why_verify_the_signature&quot;&gt;Why verify the signature?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GPG signature verification is a fundamental act of digital security. It allows:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Guarantee&lt;strong&gt;authenticity&lt;/strong&gt;of the downloaded software&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prevent the installation of a file compromised by a malicious actor&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Participate in the&lt;strong&gt;digital sovereignty&lt;/strong&gt;individual&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Promote a responsible and ethical digital culture&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;usecase-tor-verification.svg&quot; alt=&quot;usecase tor verification&quot; width=&quot;408&quot; height=&quot;263&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_extracting_and_launching_tor_browser&quot;&gt;Extracting and launching Tor Browser&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Extract the downloaded archive:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;tar -xvf tor-browser-linux-x86_64-14.5.7.tar.xz
cd tor-browser&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Then launch the browser:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;./start-tor-browser.desktop&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On the first launch, a configuration window will open to establish the connection to the Tor network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_integration_with_the_ubuntu_desktop&quot;&gt;Integration with the Ubuntu desktop&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To add &lt;strong&gt;Tor Browser&lt;/strong&gt; to the applications menu:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;./start-tor-browser.desktop --register-app&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can then:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Launch &lt;strong&gt;Tor Browser&lt;/strong&gt; from the applications menu&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Add it to dock favorites&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create a keyboard shortcut if desired&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;activity-tor-installation.svg&quot; alt=&quot;activity tor installation&quot; width=&quot;457&quot; height=&quot;470&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_explore_educational_resources_with_tor&quot;&gt;Explore educational resources with Tor&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tor is not only an anonymity tool. It constitutes an access portal to educational and research resources, notably in the fields of :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OSINT (Open Source Intelligence)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://inteltechniques.com&quot;&gt;https://inteltechniques.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://osintframework.com&quot;&gt;https://osintframework.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Educational sharing and open source&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://archive.org&quot;&gt;https://archive.org&lt;/a&gt;(access via Tor for more privacy)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/&quot; class=&quot;bare&quot;&gt;https://github.com/&lt;/a&gt;[python&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;import sys sys.stdout.write(sys.stdin.read())](accessible via Tor)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://librarygenesis.pro&quot;&gt;https://librarygenesis.pro&lt;/a&gt;(access to free scientific literature)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transmission of knowledge and understanding of humanity in the digital society&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Resources on digital culture, freedom of expression, and access to knowledge&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Free documentation on cybersecurity and technology ethics&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_updating_tor_browser&quot;&gt;Updating Tor Browser&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To ensure optimal security, it is crucial to keep &lt;strong&gt;Tor Browser&lt;/strong&gt; up to date. The browser includes an automatic update mechanism that can be triggered from the command line.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From the Tor Browser installation directory, simply restart the startup script:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-bash hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;bash&quot;&gt;cd ~/workspace/tipiak/tor/tor-browser
./start-tor-browser.desktop&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On launch, &lt;strong&gt;Tor Browser&lt;/strong&gt; will automatically check whether there is a new version. If so, it will download and install it for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This simple method ensures you always have the latest security patches and the most recent improvements, which is essential for secure browsing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_conclusion&quot;&gt;Conclusion&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Checking your downloads is an essential reflex for anyone wishing to evolve in a safe digital environment. Installing Tor in a verified manner, it is&lt;strong&gt;protect one&amp;#8217;s digital integrity&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;preserve trust in free software&lt;/strong&gt;, et &lt;strong&gt;strengthen its informational autonomy&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Digital security is an act of conscience, not of paranoia.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;summary-diagram.svg&quot; alt=&quot;summary diagram&quot; width=&quot;442&quot; height=&quot;203&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
