&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_introduction&quot;&gt;Introduction&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Target audience :&lt;/em&gt; Developers, technical writers, and anyone who wishes to write technical documentation or rich articles.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AsciiDoc is a lightweight markup language, designed for writing structured technical documents, articles, books, or even presentations. It stands out for its readability, syntactic richness, and ability to generate various formats (HTML, PDF, DocBook, etc.). In this article, we will explore the essential syntax of AsciiDoc and suggest tips for quick onboarding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_what_is_asciidoc&quot;&gt;What is AsciiDoc?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AsciiDoc is a document description language, similar to Markdown but more powerful. It allows efficient structuring of texts, headings, lists, tables, code blocks, and much more. Its versatility makes it a popular choice for documenting open‑source projects, writing books, and publishing on the web.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_why_choose_asciidoc&quot;&gt;Why choose AsciiDoc?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;olist arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;ol class=&quot;arabic&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Readable and intuitive syntax.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Native support for complex structures (tables, notes, admonitions, etc.).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Multi-format generation (HTML, PDF, ePub, DocBook…).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Easy integration with static site generators like JBake or Antora.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Advanced customization with the attributes and extensions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_use_case_diagram_use_case&quot;&gt;Use case diagram (Use Case)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A use case diagram allows presenting the main interactions between users and the system. Here is a simple example for a documentation system:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;diag-plantuml-md5-381f40e6e0660c0c53433ff054330b76.png&quot; alt=&quot;Diagram&quot; width=&quot;423&quot; height=&quot;258&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_diagram_mind_map&quot;&gt;Diagram Mind Map&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The mind map (mental map) is ideal for exploring concepts related to AsciiDoc and their relations:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;diag-plantuml-md5-e1560e9cc014158b6fbeed1e5ad8e138.png&quot; alt=&quot;Diagram&quot; width=&quot;394&quot; height=&quot;527&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_diagram_of_flow_flow&quot;&gt;Diagram of Flow (flow)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A flow diagram can be used to describe the process of generating an AsciiDoc document :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;imageblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;img src=&quot;diag-plantuml-md5-51318d77b9e18062d3a9b751587670ae.png&quot; alt=&quot;Diagram&quot; width=&quot;299&quot; height=&quot;361&quot;&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_basic_structure_of_an_asciidoc_file&quot;&gt;Basic structure of an AsciiDoc file&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An AsciiDoc file typically starts with a title, optional attributes, then the structured content. Here is a minimal example:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-asciidoc hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;asciidoc&quot;&gt;= Titre Principal
Auteur
2024-09-03
:toc:
:icons: font

Votre contenu commence ici...&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_fundamental_syntax&quot;&gt;Fundamental syntax&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_titles_and_sections&quot;&gt;Titles and sections&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AsciiDoc supports multiple heading levels:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-asciidoc hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;asciidoc&quot;&gt;= Titre de niveau 1
== Titre de niveau 2
=== Titre de niveau 3
==== Titre de niveau 4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_text_in_bold_italic_and_monospace&quot;&gt;Text in bold, italic and monospace&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-asciidoc hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;asciidoc&quot;&gt;*gras* _italique_ `monospace`&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_bullet_and_numbered_lists&quot;&gt;Bullet and numbered lists&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-asciidoc hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;asciidoc&quot;&gt;* Élément 1
* Élément 2

. Premier
. Deuxième
. Troisième&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_links_and_images&quot;&gt;Links and images&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-asciidoc hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;asciidoc&quot;&gt;Lien standard : https://asciidoc.org[AsciiDoc]
Image : image::images/logo.png[AsciiDoc Logo]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_code_blocks&quot;&gt;Code blocks&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-asciidoc hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;asciidoc&quot;&gt;[source,python]&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;def hello(): print(&quot;Hello AsciiDoc !&quot;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_tables&quot;&gt;tables&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-asciidoc hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;asciidoc&quot;&gt;|===
| Colonne 1 | Colonne 2

| Valeur A
| Valeur B

| Valeur C
| Valeur D
|===&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect2&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;_notes_and_admonitions&quot;&gt;Notes and admonitions&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AsciiDoc offers visual information blocks:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-asciidoc hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;asciidoc&quot;&gt;NOTE: Ceci est une note importante.
TIP: Conseil utile pour l’utilisateur.
WARNING: Attention à ce point.&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_use_of_attributes_and_variables&quot;&gt;Use of attributes and variables&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Custom attributes allow you to reuse values or configure behaviors:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;listingblock&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;highlightjs highlight&quot;&gt;&lt;code class=&quot;language-asciidoc hljs&quot; data-lang=&quot;asciidoc&quot;&gt;:project-name: AsciiDoc Explorer

Le projet s’appelle {project-name}.&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_common_use_cases&quot;&gt;Common use cases&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Open source project documentation (README, technical guides) - Writing books and ebooks - Automatic generation of static websites (JBake, Antora) - Technical presentations&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_best_practices&quot;&gt;Best practices&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use consistent titles and an automatic table of contents (:toc:). - Prioritize admonitions to draw attention to key points. Structure your files to facilitate maintenance. - Take advantage of annotated code blocks to illustrate examples.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_conclusion&quot;&gt;Conclusion&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AsciiDoc is a powerful and accessible tool for writing any technical documentation or structured article. Its rich syntax, combined with multi‑format generation, makes it a valuable ally for demanding developers and writers. Try AsciiDoc in your next project and discover the difference!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sect1&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;_to_go_further&quot;&gt;To go further&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;sectionbody&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;ulist&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Official documentation : &lt;a href=&quot;https://asciidoc.org&quot; class=&quot;bare&quot;&gt;https://asciidoc.org&lt;/a&gt; - Asciidoctor: &lt;a href=&quot;https://asciidoctor.org&quot; class=&quot;bare&quot;&gt;https://asciidoctor.org&lt;/a&gt; - JBake and AsciiDoc: &lt;a href=&quot;https://jbake.org/docs/2.6.4/#asciidoc_support&quot; class=&quot;bare&quot;&gt;https://jbake.org/docs/2.6.4/#asciidoc_support&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;paragraph&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Share your experiences and tips in the comments!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

